helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Java Platform Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0650.xhp\" name=\"Java Platform Support\"\>Java Platform Support\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	cy	$[officename] supports the Java platform for running applications, applets and components based on the JavaBeans architecture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	cy	For $[officename] to support the Java platform, you must install the Java 2 Runtime Environment software from Sun Microsystems. When you installed $[officename], you automatically received the option to install these files if they were not yet installed. You can also install these files now if required. The executable setup file is located in the $[officename]/program folder and on the $[officename] CD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	cy	The Java platform support needs to be activated under $[officename] to run Java applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
