helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	cy	"Alternative entry" refers to the index entry that you want to appear in the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	cy	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	cy	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	cy	"Word only" searches for the term as a single word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	cy	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	cy	To create a concordance file without the Edit Concordance File dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644				0	cy	Use the following format guidelines when you create a concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	cy	Each entry in the concordance file is on a separate line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	cy	Commented lines start with #.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	cy	Use the following format for the entries:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	cy	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270				0	cy	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	cy	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	cy	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383				0	cy	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	cy	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	cy	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
