helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGEBUTTON:TP_ENV_ENV:BTN_INSERT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database field containing the address data that you want to insert, and then click the left arrow button. The data is added to the address box containing the cursor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Current Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06160000.xhp\" name=\"Current Index\"\>Current Index\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UpdateCurIndex\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates the current index.\</ahelp\> The current index is the one that contains the cursor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	cy	You can also right-click in an index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>. The following commands are also available in the context menu:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146967				0	cy	Edit Index/Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditCurIndex\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Edits the current index or table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147403				0	cy	Delete Index/Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RemoveTableOf\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Deletes the current index or table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Page Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Formatting\"\>Page Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	cy	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:Repaginate\"\>Updates the page formats in the document and recalculates the total number of pages that is displayed on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	cy	In long documents, updating the page formatting can take a while.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149123				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Functions\"\>Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets additional function parameters for fields. The type of parameter depends on the field type that you select.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	cy	Depending on the field type that you select, you can assign conditions to certain functions. For example, you can define a field that executes a macro when you click the field in the document, or a condition that, when met, hides a field. You can also define placeholder fields that insert graphics, tables, frames and other objects into your document when needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	cy	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155623				0	cy	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	cy	Conditional text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881	6			0	cy	Inserts text if a certain \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> is met. For example, enter "sun eq 1" in the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, and then the text that you want to insert when the variable "sun" equals "1" in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box. If you want, you can also enter the text that you want to display when this condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else\</emph\> box. To define the variable "sun", click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>\<emph\>Variables\</emph\>\</link\> tab, select "Set variable", type "sun" in the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, and its value in the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153719				0	cy	Input list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147564				0	cy	Inserts a text field that displays one item from a list. You can add, edit, and remove items, and change their order in the list. Click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in your document or press Ctrl+Shift+F9 to display the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Choose Item\"\>\<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	cy	Input field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	cy	Inserts a text field that you can open by \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"clicking\"\>clicking\</link\> it in the document. You can then change the text that is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154691				0	cy	Execute macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	10			0	cy	Inserts a text field that runs a macro when you click the field in the document. To assign a macro to the field, click the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	cy	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	cy	Inserts a placeholder field in the document, for example, for graphics. When you click a placeholder field in the document, you are prompted to insert the item that is missing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973				0	cy	Hidden text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	cy	Hidden Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192	39			0	cy	Combine characters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3159199				0	cy	Combines up to 6 characters, so that they behave as a single character. This feature is only available when Asian fonts are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151329				0	cy	For function fields, the format field is only used for fields of the type placeholder. Here, the format determines the object for which the placeholder stands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149494				0	cy	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBCONDITION\"\>For fields linked to a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151248				0	cy	Then, Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	21			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCCOND2\"\>Enter the text to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, and the text to display when the condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	22			0	cy	You can also insert database fields in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>and \<emph\>Else \</emph\>boxes using the format "databasename.tablename.fieldname".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583				0	cy	If the table or the field name does not exist in a database, nothing is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585				0	cy	If you include the quotes in "databasename.tablename.fieldname", the expression is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155136				0	cy	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155149	27			0	cy	Type the text that you want to display in the field. If you are inserting a placeholder field, type the text that you want to display as a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
