helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157557				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020100.xhp\" name=\"Section\"\>Section\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	cy	Sets the properties of the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151170				0	cy	New Section				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:ED_RNAME\"\>Type a name for the new section.\</ahelp\> By default, $[officename] automatically assigns the name "Section X" to new sections, where X is a consecutive number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154102				0	cy	Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149806				0	cy	Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:CB_FILE\"\>Inserts the contents of another document or section from another document in the current section.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153672				0	cy	DDE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151310	27			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_DDE\"\>Creates a \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>link. Select this check box, and then enter the \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>command that you want to use. The \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> option is only available if the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box is selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143280				0	cy	The general syntax for a DDE command is: "<Server> <Topic> <Item>", where server is the DDE name for the application that contains the data. Topic refers to the location of the Item (usually the file name), and Item represents the actual object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098	35			0	cy	For example, to insert a section named "Section1" from a $[officename] text document abc.sxw as a DDE link, use the command: "soffice x:\\abc.sxw Section1". To insert the contents of the first cell from a MS Excel spreadsheet file called "abc.xls", use the command: "excel x:\\[abc.xls]Sheet1 z1s1". You can also copy the elements that you want to insert as a DDE link, and then \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. You can then view the DDE command for the link, by selecting the contents and choosing \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153640	28			0	cy	File name\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> / DDE command \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145754	29			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:MD_EDIT_REGION:ED_FILE\"\>Enter the path and the filename for the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) to locate the file.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>check box is selected, enter the DDE command that you want to use. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156274				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:MD_EDIT_REGION:PB_FILE\"\>Locate the file that you want to insert as a link, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	cy	Section				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:LB_SUBREG\"\>Select the section in the file that you want to insert as a link.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151373				0	cy	When you open a document that contains linked sections, you are prompted to update the links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150687				0	cy	Write Protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150700				0	cy	Protected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents the selected section from being edited.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145261				0	cy	With password				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_INSERT_SECTION_CB_PASSWD\"\>Protects the selected section with a password. The password must have a minimum of 5 characters.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147742				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_INSERT_SECTION_PB_PASSWD\"\>Opens a dialog where you can change the current password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146333				0	cy	Hide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149830				0	cy	Hide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148849				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_HIDE\"\>Hides and prevents the selected section from being printed.\</ahelp\> The components of a hidden sections appear gray in the Navigator. When you rest your mouse pointer over a hidden component in the Navigator, the Help tip "hidden" is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155074				0	cy	You cannot hide a section if it is the only content on a page, or in a header, footer, footnote, frame, or table cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154323				0	cy	With condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154343				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:MD_EDIT_REGION:ED_CONDITION\"\>Enter the condition that must be met to hide the section.\</ahelp\> A condition is a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"logical expression\"\>logical expression\</link\>, such as "SALUTATION EQ Mr.". For example, if you use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"mail merge\"\>mail merge\</link\> form letter feature to define a database field called "Salutation" that contains "Mr.", "Ms.", or "Sir or Madam", you can then specify that a section will only be printed if the salutation is "Mr.".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	cy	Another example would be to create the field variable "x" and set its value to 1. Then specify a condition based on this variable for hiding a section, such as: "x eq 1". If you want to display the section, set the value of the variable "x" to "0".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DF				0	cy	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E3				0	cy	You see this area of the dialog when the current document is an XForms document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E6				0	cy	Editable in read-only document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN108EA				0	cy	Select to allow editing of the section's contents even if the document is opened in read-only mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150032				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Field commands\"\>Field commands\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3158420				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Syntax for conditions\"\>Syntax for conditions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287				0	cy	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	cy	\<variable id=\"optionentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_CAPTION:BTN_OPTION\"\>Adds the chapter number to the caption label. To use this feature, you must first assign an \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"outline level\"\>outline level\</link\> to a paragraph style, and then apply the style to the chapter headings in your document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149805				0	cy	Numbering by chapter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153532				0	cy	When you add chapter numbers to caption labels, the caption numbering is reset when a chapter heading is encountered. For example, if the last figure in chapter 1 is "Figure 1.12", the first figure in the next chapter would be "Figure 2.1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154574				0	cy	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152954				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_SEQUENCE_OPTION:LB_LEVEL\"\>Select the number of outline levels from the top of the chapter hierarchy down to include in the caption label.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151316				0	cy	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_SEQUENCE_OPTION:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>Enter the character that you want to insert between the chapter number and the caption number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
