helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154561				0	cy	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	cy	\<variable id=\"kapnum\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChapterNumberingDialog\"\>Specifies the number format and the hierarchy for chapter numbering in the current document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934				0	cy	Outline numbering is linked to paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading" paragraph styles (1-10) are assigned to the corresponding outline number levels (1-10). If you want, you can assign different paragraph styles to the outline number level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147567	55			0	cy	To highlight the screen display of outline numbers, choose \<emph\>View -\</emph\>\<emph\>Field Shadings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151168				0	cy	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OUTLINE_FORM\"\>Saves or loads an outline number format. A saved outline number format is available to all text documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	cy	The \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button is only available for outline numbering. For numbered or bulleted list styles, modify the Numbering Styles of the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154572				0	cy	Untitled 1 - 9				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NAMED_NUMS\"\>Select the predefined numbering style that you want to assign to the selected outline level.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153675				0	cy	Save As				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NUM_SAVEAS\"\>Opens a dialog where you can save the current settings for the selected outline level. You can then load these settings from another document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	cy	Save As				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_NUM_NAMES:LB_FORM\"\>Click a numbering style in the list, and then enter a name for the style. The numbers correspond to the outline level that the styles are assigned to.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Optimal Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149500				0	cy	Optimal Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149050				0	cy	\<variable id=\"spaltenbreitetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SetOptimalColumnWidth\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Automatically adjusts column widths to match the contents of the cells.\</ahelp\> Changing the width of a column does not affect the width of the other columns in the table. The width of the table cannot exceed the page width.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154656				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>styles; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154656				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130100.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>Condition\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	cy	Define conditions for conditional styles here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	cy	Conditional styles are paragraph styles that have different properties depending on the context. Once defined, you cannot change the conditional properties of a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349				0	cy	$[officename] applies the paragraph properties of conditional styles as follows (the bold terms correspond to the titles of dialog fields): If a paragraph formatted with a conditional style is in a \<emph\>Context\</emph\> that has an \<emph\>Applied Style\</emph\> linked to it, then the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> from that condition is used. If no style is linked to the \<emph\>Context\</emph\>, then the attributes defined in the conditional style apply. The following example illustrates this relationship:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	cy	Open a blank text document and write a short business letter with a header (\<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<emph\>Page\</emph\> - \<emph\>Header\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148768				0	cy	Define a new Paragraph Style by choosing \<emph\>New\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and selecting all the paragraph properties that you want for your business letter in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog. Name this style "Business letter".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153723				0	cy	Then click the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> tab and select the \<emph\>Conditional style\</emph\> field to define the new Paragraph Style as a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154647				0	cy	In \<emph\>Context\</emph\>, select the header entry and under \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> select the style for the header in your business letter; for example, the default Paragraph Style "Header". You also can select your own style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150760				0	cy	You can apply the Paragraph Style to the context by double-clicking the selected entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> list box or by using \<emph\>Assign\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149753				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the Paragraph Style dialog, and then format all paragraphs in your business letter, including the header, with the new "Business letter" conditional Paragraph Style. (When you click in the header, you may need to display \<item type=\"literal\"\>All Styles\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>Custom Styles\</item\> in the style list to use the new business letter style.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412				0	cy	The header text now has the attributes you specified in the Header Paragraph Style, while the other parts of the document have the attributes defined in the business letter conditional Paragraph Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154473				0	cy	The "Text body" Style was created as a conditional style. Therefore, any styles you derive from it can be used as conditional styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	cy	The Paragraph Style applied to the context is used when exporting to other formats (RTF, HTML, and so on).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	cy	Conditional style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150974				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_CONDCOLL:CB_CONDITION\"\>Check this box to define a new style as a conditional style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153672				0	cy	Context				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_COND_COLL_TABLIST\"\>Here you can see the $[officename] predefined contexts, including outline levels 1 to 10, numbering/bullets levels 1 to 10, table header, table contents, section, border, footnote, header and footer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155896				0	cy	Applied Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149689				0	cy	Here you can see the list of all Paragraph Styles applied to a context.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154194				0	cy	Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159195				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_CONDCOLL:LB_STYLE\"\>A list of all Paragraph Styles which can be assigned to a context is contained in the list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149306				0	cy	Remove				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151335				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_CONDCOLL:PB_REMOVE\"\>Click here to remove the current context assigned to the selected style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149483				0	cy	Assign				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_CONDCOLL:PB_ASSIGN\"\>Click \<emph\>Assign\</emph\> to apply the \<emph\>selected Paragraph Style\</emph\> to the defined \<emph\>context\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Create AutoAbstract				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148570				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01160300.xhp\" name=\"Create AutoAbstract\"\>Create AutoAbstract\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286	2			0	cy	\<variable id=\"autoabstracttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CreateAbstract\"\>Copies the headings and a number of subsequent paragraphs in the active document to a new AutoAbstract text document. An AutoAbstract is useful for obtaining an overview of long documents.\</ahelp\> You can specify the number of outline levels as well as the number of paragraphs displayed therein. All levels and paragraphs under the respective settings are hidden. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147516				0	cy	Included Outline Levels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149804				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_INSERT_ABSTRACT:NF_LEVEL\"\>Enter the extent of the outline levels to be copied to the new document.\</ahelp\> For example, if you choose 4 levels, all paragraphs formatted with Heading 1 to Heading 4 are included, along with the number of subsequent paragraphs specified in \<emph\>Subpoints per Level\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151316				0	cy	Subpoints per Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_INSERT_ABSTRACT:NF_PARA\"\>Specify the maximum number of consecutive paragraphs to be included in the AutoAbstract document after each heading.\</ahelp\> All of the paragraphs up to the maximum defined are included until the next paragraph with a Heading Style is reached.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06210000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Links				2002-02-02 02:02:02
