helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using Captions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147691				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>captions; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; as captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labeling draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	cy	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	cy	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	cy	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	cy	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	cy	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	cy	Defining Captions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	cy	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	cy	Select the options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<emph\>Category \</emph\>box, for example "Figure".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	cy	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	cy	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption \<emph\>Category\</emph\>. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Numbering and Numbering Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; manually/by styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual numbering in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles;numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering styles;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;numbering styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174	30			0	cy	\<variable id=\"using_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Numbering and Numbering Styles\"\>Numbering and Numbering Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149818				0	cy	You can apply numbering to a paragraph manually or with a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	cy	To apply numbering manually, click in the paragraph, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153405				0	cy	You cannot apply manual numbering to paragraphs that are listed under "Special Styles" in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10711				0	cy	When you press Enter in a numbered or bulleted list, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically numbers the next paragraph. To remove the numbering or bullet from the new paragraph, press Enter again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	cy	To change the hierarchical level of a bullet in a list, click in front of the paragraph, then press the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072F				0	cy	To change the bullets or numbering format for the current paragraph only, select a character or word in the paragraph, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10733				0	cy	To change the bullet or numbering format for all paragraphs in the list, ensure that the cursor is in the list, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	cy	To apply the same bullet or numbering format to all paragraphs in the list, select all paragraphs, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073A				0	cy	You can also use the commands on the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Object Bar\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> toolbar to edit a numbered or bulleted list. To change the numbering or bullet format, click the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153123				0	cy	To apply numbering with a Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153137				0	cy	Paragraph Styles give you greater control over numbering that you apply in a document. When you change the numbering format of the style, all paragraphs using the style are automatically updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	cy	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to apply numbering to, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149850				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Numbering Styles\</emph\> box, select the type of numbering that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	cy	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Hiding Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>comparisons; hidden text fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden text; displaying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden paragraphs; text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-printing text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; only showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying;hidden text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	cy	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	cy	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	cy	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	cy	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	cy	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	cy	Type a name for the variable in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box, for example, "Hide".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	cy	Enter a value for the variable in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box, for example, "1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	cy	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	cy	To hide text:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	cy	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	cy	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	cy	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	cy	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	cy	To hide a paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	cy	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	cy	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	cy	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675				0	cy	To hide a section:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	cy	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	cy	In the\<emph\> Hide\</emph\> area, select\<emph\> Hide\</emph\>, and then enter an expression in the\<emph\> Condition\</emph\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
