helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;text sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;links, manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	cy	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	cy	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	cy	To insert a new section:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	cy	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	cy	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	cy	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	cy	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	cy	To insert a section as a link:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	cy	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	cy	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	cy	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browsers, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	cy	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	cy	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	cy	Click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) next to the \<emph\>File name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	cy	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Section \</emph\>box, select the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; index format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; formatting indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; hyperlinks as entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; in tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;indexes and tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	cy	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	cy	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	cy	To apply a different paragraph style to an index level:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	cy	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	cy	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	cy	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	cy	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	cy	To assign hyperlinks to entries in a table of contents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	cy	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	cy	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	cy	Click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to in the \<emph\>Level \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	cy	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	cy	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<emph\>All levels\</emph\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Converting a Field into Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154079				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>fields; converting into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;fields, into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;fields, by text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;fields, into text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154079				0	cy	\<variable id=\"field_convert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/field_convert.xhp\" name=\"Converting a Field into Text\"\>Converting a Field into Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	cy	You can change a field to regular text, so that it is no longer updated. After you change a field to text, you cannot change the text back into a field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155608				0	cy	Select the field and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154238				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	cy	Click "Unformatted text" in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\field_convert.xhp	0	help	par_id3157551				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	cy	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	cy	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	cy	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	cy	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	cy	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	cy	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	cy	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	cy	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	cy	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	cy	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	cy	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	cy	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	cy	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	cy	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	cy	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	cy	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	cy	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Repeating a Table Header on a New Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155870				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>table headings; repeating after page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating; table headings after page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; repeating in tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153406				0	cy	\<variable id=\"table_repeat_multiple_headers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp\" name=\"Repeating a Table Header on a New Page\"\>Repeating a Table Heading on a New Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149636				0	cy	You can repeat a table heading on each new page that the table spans.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Table - Insert - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	cy	Select the \<emph\>Heading \</emph\>and the \<emph\>Repeat heading \</emph\>check boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	cy	Select the number of rows and columns for the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153393				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Formatting Headers or Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; lines under headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	cy	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	cy	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page \</emph\>and select the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>or \<emph\>Footer \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	cy	Set the spacing options that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	cy	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Border/Background \</emph\>dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	cy	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	cy	Under \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\>, select \<emph\>Portrait\</emph\> or \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	cy	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page orientation of one or more pages in a document from portrait to landscape in a document, you need to create a page style that uses the landscape orientation, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	cy	Right-click, and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	cy	Under \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\>, select \<emph\>Portrait\</emph\> or \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	About Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	cy	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	cy	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	cy	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	cy	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	cy	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	cy	You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> or \<emph\>Footer \</emph\>tab, and then select \<emph\>Header on \</emph\>or \<emph\>Footer on\</emph\>. Clear the \<emph\>Same content left/right\</emph\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	cy	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	cy	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	cy	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Online Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	cy	 Inserting an additional space character 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	cy	 Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	cy	 The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	cy	 Selecting the accept key 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	cy	 Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	cy	 Selecting the number of characters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	cy	 Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	cy	 Selecting the scope of collected words 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	cy	 Select \<emph\>When closing a document, save the list for later use in other documents\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	cy	 Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	cy	 If you do not select the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	cy	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	cy	 Working with the word list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	cy	 If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	cy	 Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	cy	 Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	cy	 The word completion feature collects the words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	cy	 Select all or some of the words in the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	cy	 Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\"\>Word Completion \</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Templates and Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	cy	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	cy	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, object, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	cy	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the "Default" template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	cy	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	cy	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	cy	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	cy	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	cy	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	cy	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	cy	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	cy	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	cy	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
