helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	cy	To hide the borders of the frame, select the frame, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab, and then click in the\<emph\> Set No Border\</emph\> box in the\<emph\> Line Arrangement\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	cy	To resize the frame, drag the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;mean values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	cy	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	cy	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	cy	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	cy	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	cy	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	cy	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	cy	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating directly in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula bar in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	cy	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	cy	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	cy	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	cy	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, "=10000/12", and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	cy	You can also click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; size of text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linking frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;not printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text from printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	cy	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	cy	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	cy	Inserting Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	cy	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	cy	Editing Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	cy	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	cy	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	cy	To resize a text frame, click an edge of frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	cy	Hiding Text From Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	cy	Any text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	cy	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	cy	Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	cy	You can link text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	cy	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	cy	On the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> Bar, click the \<emph\>Link Frames\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	cy	Click the frame that you want to link to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	cy	You can only link frames if:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	cy	The target frame is empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	cy	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	cy	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	cy	The source frame does not have a next link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	cy	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	cy	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using Rulers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indent settings on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	cy	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	cy	Adjusting Page Margins				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	cy	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	cy	Changing Indents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	cy	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	cy	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	cy	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	cy	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154922				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting pictures in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922				0	cy	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149695				0	cy	There are several ways to insert a graphic object in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	cy	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the sum of a series of table cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	cy	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	cy	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<emph\>Sum\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.\<br/\>The\<emph\> Formula Bar\</emph\> appears with the entry "=sum".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	cy	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	cy	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	cy	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	cy	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>headers; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>creating; page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	cy	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	cy	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	cy	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	cy	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	cy	Type a name for the page in the \<emph\>Style name \</emph\>box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	cy	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	cy	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\> and then select 'Default' from the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	cy	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom \<emph\>Page Style\</emph\> with a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
