helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	cy	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	cy	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	cy	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	cy	Cross-Referencing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	cy	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	cy	To insert a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	cy	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select \<emph\>Set Reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	cy	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The name of the target is added to the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	cy	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	cy	To create a cross-reference to a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	cy	Cross-Referencing an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	cy	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	cy	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	cy	Updating Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	cy	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; page styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	cy	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	cy	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	cy	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	cy	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	cy	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	cy	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	cy	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	cy	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	cy	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	cy	If you want do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Going to Specific Bookmark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145778				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; positioning cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>jumping to bookmarks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	cy	\<variable id=\"jump2statusbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/jump2statusbar.xhp\" name=\"Going to Specific Bookmark\"\>Going to Specific Bookmark\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178	31			0	cy	To go to a specific bookmark in your document, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>hold down Ctrl and click \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>right-click\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> field on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>, and then choose the bookmark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Bookmark\"\>Insert Bookmark\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Word Completion for Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>switching off word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	cy	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	cy	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	cy	 Using word completion 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	cy	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	cy	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	cy	 Switching off the word completion 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	cy	 Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Word Completion\</emph\> . 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	cy	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>modifying;numbering in lists\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	cy	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	cy	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	cy	To remove the number from a paragraph in a numbered list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	cy	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	cy	To change the number that a numbered list starts with:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	cy	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	cy	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<emph\>Start at\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Printing Register-true				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	bm_id4825891				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>rows; register-true text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines of text;register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages;register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>register-true;pages and paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spacing;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	cy	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	cy	Setting a document to register-true printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	cy	Select the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	cy	Select the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	cy	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	cy	Exempting paragraphs from register-true printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	cy	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	cy	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	cy	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
