helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>multicolumn text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; multicolumn\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections; remarks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	cy	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	cy	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	cy	To prevent text from being edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	cy	To show or hide text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	cy	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	cy	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	cy	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	cy	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	cy	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	cy	Sections and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	cy	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	cy	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147688				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;words in user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147688				0	cy	\<variable id=\"delete_from_dict\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/delete_from_dict.xhp\" name=\"Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\"\>Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	cy	Select the user-defined dictionary that you want to edit in the \<emph\>User-defined \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	cy	Select the word that you want to delete in the \<emph\>Word\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode; in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	cy	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	cy	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	cy	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	cy	Click the style, and then click the \<emph\>Fill Format Mode\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	cy	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	cy	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
