helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	cy	\<variable id=\"pagebackground\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Changing Page Background\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	cy	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the background of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page background of one or more pages in a document to a watermark, you need to create a page style that uses the watermark background, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	cy	To Change the Page Background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	cy	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085F				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	cy	In the list box at the top, select whether you want a solid color or a graphic. Then select your options from the tab page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086B				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087A				0	cy	To Change the Page Background of All Pages in a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	cy	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089A				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	cy	Double-click the page style that uses the page background that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	cy	To Use Different Page Backgrounds in the Same Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A9				0	cy	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	cy	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
