helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>headers; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	cy	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	cy	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	cy	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Page\</emph\> tab, and in the\<emph\> Layout settings\</emph\> area, choose\<emph\> Mirrored\</emph\> in the\<emph\> Page layout\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	cy	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	cy	Open a new text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	cy	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	cy	Select\<emph\> Header on\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Next Style \</emph\>box, select "Left Page".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	cy	Select\<emph\> Header on\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Next Style \</emph\>box, select "Right Page".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	cy	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	cy	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>words; do not hyphenate\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separation, see hyphenation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>word wrapping for text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	cy	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	cy	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864				0	cy	Automatic hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	cy	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	cy	To automatically hyphenate text in a paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	cy	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	cy	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149629				0	cy	To automatically hyphenate text in multiple paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	cy	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	cy	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	cy	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145106				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Text Flow \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145400				0	cy	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	cy	Manual Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	cy	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	cy	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	cy	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154847				0	cy	To manually hyphenate text in a selection:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	cy	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152999				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>charts; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; charts from $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting Calc charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152999				0	cy	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\"\>Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155890				0	cy	You can insert a copy of a chart that is not updated when you modify the chart data in the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	cy	Open the text document that you want to copy the chart to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	cy	Open the spreadsheet containing the chart that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	cy	In the spreadsheet, click the chart. Eight handles appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	cy	Drag the chart from the spreadsheet to the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	cy	You can resize and move the chart in the text document as you would any object. To edit the chart data, double-click the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149689				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; defining in indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	cy	\<variable id=\"indices_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_enter.xhp\" name=\"Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\"\>Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155862				0	cy	Defining Index Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	cy	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119				0	cy	Defining Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147132				0	cy	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. You can also use custom paragraph styles, so long as you assign them one of the predefined outline levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230				0	cy	To use a custom paragraph style as a table of contents entry:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	cy	Select the paragraph style that you want to include in your table of contents in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Level\</emph\> list, click the hierarchical level that you want to apply the paragraph style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730	17			0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You can now apply the style to headings in your document and include them in your table of contents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Navigator for Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
