helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149489				0	cy	\<variable id=\"table_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_delete.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\"\>Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	cy	You can delete a table from your document, or delete the contents of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155863				0	cy	To delete a whole table, click in the table, and then choose \<emph\>Table - Delete - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	cy	To delete the contents of a table, click in the table, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all cells are selected, and then press Delete or Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152887				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; adding exceptions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exceptions; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887				0	cy	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	cy	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Exceptions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	cy	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	cy	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	cy	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
