helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147418	15			0	cy	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists2.xhp\" name=\"Adding Numbering\"\>Adding Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	cy	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968	24			0	cy	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar, click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153125\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_defaultnumbering.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153125\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149573				0	cy	To change the formatting and the hierarchy of a numbered list, click in the list, and then open the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	cy	To remove numbering, select the numbered paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154233				0	cy	Formatting a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	cy	To change the formatting of a numbered list, click in the list, then choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Moving and Copying Text in Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>text sections; moving and copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;moving and copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; text sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; text sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mouse;moving and copying text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	cy	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	cy	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	cy	To create a master document: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	cy	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	cy	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<emph\>Move down\</emph\> or \<emph\>Move up \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	cy	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	cy	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	cy	To start each subdocument on a new page:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	cy	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	cy	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	cy	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Text Flow \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Breaks \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then select \<emph\>Page \</emph\>in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	cy	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	cy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	About Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>fields; using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	cy	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	cy	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	cy	Viewing Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	cy	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	cy	Field Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	cy	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	cy	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	cy	Field Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	cy	Property				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	cy	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	cy	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	cy	Insert Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	cy	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	cy	Run macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	cy	Runs a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	cy	Input Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	cy	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	cy	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the \<emph\>Extended Tips \</emph\>option is selected in the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	cy	Updating Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	cy	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	cy	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	cy	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	cy	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	cy	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	cy	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	cy	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon, and ensure that \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink \</emph\>is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	cy	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	cy	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	cy	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	cy	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
