helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Compatibility				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3577990				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>Word documents;compatibility\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;compatibility settings for text import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;compatibility\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compatibility;options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compatibility; MS Word\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;printer metrics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metrics;document formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printer metrics for document formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10607				0	cy	\<variable id=\"compatibility_var\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041000.xhp\"\>Compatibility\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10625				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"53251\"\>Specifies compatibility settings for text documents. These options help in fine-tuning %PRODUCTNAME when importing Microsoft Word documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	cy	Some of the settings defined here are only valid for the current document and must be defined separately for each document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	cy	Use printer metrics for document formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_PRINTER_METRICS\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155768				0	cy	If you set this option for the current document and then save the document, for example, in an older binary format, this option will not be saved. If you later open the file from the older format, this option will be set by default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640				0	cy	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	cy	In $[officename] Writer, paragraph spacing is defined differently than in MS Word documents. If you have defined spacing between two paragraphs or tables, spacing is also added in the corresponding MS Word documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST\"\>Specifies whether to add MS Word-compatible spacing between paragraphs and tables in $[officename] Writer text documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	cy	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST_PAGESTART\"\>Specifies whether paragraph spacing at the top of a page is also be effective at the beginning of a page or column if the paragraph is positioned on the first page of the document.\</ahelp\> The same applies for a page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	cy	If you import an MS Word document, the spaces are automatically added during the conversion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964				0	cy	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 tab stop formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not selected, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	cy	In text documents created by %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In documents created by %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the previously used tab stop handling is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	cy	Do not add leading (extra space) between lines of text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	cy	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	cy	In text documents created by %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, the additional leading is used by default. In documents created by %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the additional leading is not used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	cy	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 line spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	cy	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	cy	In %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the previous process is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	cy	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	cy	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	cy	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	cy	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 object positioning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	cy	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	cy	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in %PRODUCTNAME versions prior to %PRODUCTVERSION. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	cy	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	cy	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 text wrapping around objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	cy	MS Word and Writer have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen object are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in MS Word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	cy	In MS Word and in %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	cy	In %PRODUCTNAME prior to %PRODUCTVERSION, the opposite was true.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	cy	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, \<emph\>the former text wrapping will be applied.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	cy	Consider wrapping style when positioning objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	cy	Specifies how the complex iterative process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, an iterative process was used, while in %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	cy	If the option is off, the %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	cy	Use as Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10848				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"879350288\"\>Click to use the current settings on this tab page as the default for further sessions with %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10977				0	cy	The factory defaults are set as follows. Enabled are the following options, while all other options are disabled:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1097D				0	cy	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10981				0	cy	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10985				0	cy	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153823				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>Changes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_REDLINE_OPT\"\>Defines the appearance of changes in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156153				0	cy	To record or show changes, with the text or spreadsheet document open, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	cy	Text display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	cy	Defines the settings for displaying recorded changes. Select the type of change with the radio buttons, and the corresponding display attribute and color. The preview field shows the effect of the selected display options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	cy	Insertions / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_INS_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is inserted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812				0	cy	Deletions / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_DEL_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is deleted. If you record text deletions, the text is displayed with the selected attribute (for example, strikethrough) and is not deleted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148674				0	cy	Changed attributes / Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_ATTR\"\>Defines how changes to text attributes are displayed in the document. These changes affect attributes such as bold, italic or underline.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	cy	Color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_COL\"\>It is possible to select a color to identify each type of recorded change. By entering "By author" from the list, the color is automatically determined by $[officename] and modified according to the corresponding author of the changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145607				0	cy	Lines changed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	cy	To indicate which lines of the text have been changed, you can define a mark that appears in the left or right page margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	cy	Mark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_MARKPOS\"\>Defines if and where changed lines in the document are marked.\</ahelp\> You can set the markings so that they always appear on the left or right page margin, or on even or uneven pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163713				0	cy	Color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_LC_COL\"\>Specifies the color for highlighting the changed lines in the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Writing Aids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	bm_id7986388				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>writing aids;options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; editing user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exceptions; user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; dictionary of exceptions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; dictionary of exceptions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ignore list for spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; ignore list\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; German\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation; minimal number of characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>old German spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new German spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Writing Aids\"\>Writing Aids\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_LINGU\"\>Specifies the properties of the spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	cy	Available Language Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_MODULES\"\>Contains the installed language modules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153663	35			0	cy	A language module can contain one, two or three submodules: Spellcheck, hyphenation and thesaurus. Each sub-module can be available in one or more languages. If you click in front of the name of the module, you activate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you remove a set mark, you deactivate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you wish to activate or deactivate individual sub-modules, click the\<emph\> Edit button \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307				0	cy	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	37			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_MODULES_EDIT\"\>To edit a language module, select it and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153348				0	cy	User-defined dictionaries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_EDIT_MODULES_DICS\"\>Lists the available user dictionaries.\</ahelp\> Mark the user dictionaries that you want to use for spellcheck and hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144511				0	cy	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_NEW_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>New Dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	cy	New Dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	cy	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	cy	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	cy	Exceptions (-)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> You can include in the custom dictionary defined in this way all the words to be avoided. During the spellcheck, if this exception dictionary is activated, you will receive a corresponding note that this word should be avoided.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	cy	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	cy	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	cy	Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_ALLDICTS\"\>Specifies the book to be edited.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	79			0	cy	\<variable id=\"ignore\"\>The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>includes all words that have been marked with \<emph\>Ignore \</emph\>during spellcheck, This list is administered only for the current spellcheck in the volatile RAM. Some user data will be entered in the list at program start. \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>cannot be deleted. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	cy	The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList\</emph\> entry cannot be selected and cannot be deleted. Only the words included as content can be deleted. This happens automatically each time that $[officename] is closed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	cy	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>Assigns a new language to the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	cy	Word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_WORD\"\>You can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> If you select a word from this list it is displayed in the text field. If you type a word with an equals sign after it, such as "AutoComplete=", the word is neither automatically hyphenated nor is a hyphenation suggested. Typing "Auto=Complete" result in the word being hyphenated, or a hyphenation suggested, at this point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155175				0	cy	Suggestion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147323				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_REPLACE\"\>This input field is only available if you are editing an exception dictionary. The field takes the alterative suggestion for the word in the "Word" text box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	cy	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	89			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:PB_NEW_REPLACE\"\>Adds the word in the \<emph\>Word \</emph\>text field to your current custom dictionary. The word in the \<emph\>Suggestion \</emph\>field is also added when working with exception dictionaries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149032				0	cy	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_OPTIONS\"\>Defines the options for the spellcheck and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	cy	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_OPTIONS_EDIT\"\>If you want to change a value, select the entry and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You will see a dialog for entering a new value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150983				0	cy	Check uppercase words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	cy	Specifies that capitalization is checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	cy	Check words with numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	cy	Specifies that words that contain numbers as well as letters are to be checked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147509				0	cy	Check capitalization				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	cy	Checks for the correct use of capitals at the start of words during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166424				0	cy	Check special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	cy	Specifies that special regions, such as text in headers and footers, document tables, and text frames, are checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166429				0	cy	Check spelling as you type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	cy	\<variable id=\"automatisch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpellOnline\"\>Automatically checks spelling as you type, and underlines errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	cy	Typing errors are highlighted in the document with a red underline. If you place the cursor over a word marked in this way, you can open the context menu to obtain a list of suggested corrections. Select a suggested correction to replace the suspect word with the suggestion. If you make the same mistake again while editing the document, it will be corrected automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	cy	To place the word pair in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect replacement table\"\>AutoCorrect replacement table\</link\>, open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040500.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect context menu\"\>AutoCorrect context menu\</link\> and choose \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Make your selection from the submenu. The word is replaced and at the same time the word pair is placed in the replacement table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150111	53			0	cy	Minimal number of characters for hyphenation 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150316				0	cy	Specifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_LNGDLG_NUM_PREBREAK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\> Type the minimum number of characters that must come before or after the hyphen.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148823				0	cy	Characters before line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	cy	Sets the minimum number of characters of the word to be hyphenated that must remain at the end of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154956				0	cy	Characters after line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149439				0	cy	Specifies the minimum number of characters of a hyphenated word required at the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156337				0	cy	Hyphenate without inquiry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151130				0	cy	Specifies that you will never be asked for a manual hyphenation. If the field is not marked, when a word is not recognized you will be presented with a dialog for entering hyphens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155900				0	cy	Hyphenate special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155098				0	cy	Specifies that hyphenation will also be carried out in footnotes, headers and footers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147577				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>settings; proxies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proxy settings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020100.xhp\" name=\"Proxy\"\>Proxy\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"Proxy servers\"\>Proxy servers\</link\> for accessing the Internet can be set up manually as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	cy	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	cy	Defines the settings for the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"proxy server\"\>proxy server\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	cy	Proxy server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:LB_PROXYMODE\"\>Specifies the type of proxy definition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	cy	None				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	cy	Accesses the Internet without a proxy server. Allows you to set up a connection directly on your computer to an Internet provider that does not use a proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	cy	Manual				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	cy	Lets you enter the proxy server manually. Specify the proxy servers in accordance with your Internet service. Ask your system administrator for the proxies and ports to enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	cy	Type server names without the protocol prefix. For example, type www.sun.com, not http://www.sun.com.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10684				0	cy	System				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	cy	On Windows or UNIX systems using Gnome, this option tells %PRODUCTNAME to use the system settings. You must restart %PRODUCTNAME to initiate this setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148948				0	cy	HTTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_HTTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#http\" name=\"HTTP\"\>HTTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543				0	cy	FTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY_ED_FTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#ftp\" name=\"FTP\"\>FTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	cy	No proxy for				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_NOPROXYFOR\"\>Specifies the names of the servers that do not require any proxy servers, separated by semicolons.\</ahelp\> These are servers addressed in your local network, and servers used for video and audio streaming, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	cy	You can also use placeholders for the names of hosts and domains. For example, type *.sun.com to address all the hosts in the sun.com domain without proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149808				0	cy	Port				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_SOCKS_PORT\"\>Type the port for the corresponding proxy server.\</ahelp\> The maximum value of a port number is fixed at 65535.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
