helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	cy	Opening Documents With Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	40			0	cy	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> stores templates in the following directories:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144442				0	cy	the user template directory \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>in the home directory \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>in the Documents and Settings directory\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	cy	When you open a document that was created from a template, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> checks to see if the template has been modified since the document was last opened. If the template was changed a dialog is shown where you can select which styles to apply to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096				0	cy	To apply the new styles from the template to the document, click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147581				0	cy	To retain the styles that are currently used in the document, click \<emph\>No\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988				0	cy	If a document was created using a template that cannot be found a dialog is shown that asks you how to proceed next time the document is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151351				0	cy	To break the link between the document and the missing template, click \<emph\>No\</emph\>, otherwise \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> will look for the template the next time you open the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
