helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857				0	cy	You can save some passwords for the duration of a session, or permanently to a file protected by a master password. For example, passwords for accessing WebDAV or FTP servers are stored permanently if you enter a master password when prompted. Otherwise, they are only stored for the current session.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3147000				0	cy	You must enter the master password to access a file or service that is protected by a saved password. You only need to enter the master password once during a session.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
