helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialog, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	cy	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	cy	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>margins; setting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; setting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13020000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\"\>Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	cy	You can define the indents and margins for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	cy	If you split the page into columns, or the cursor is placed in a multiple-column text frame, you can change the column width and the column spacing by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	cy	When an object, an image, or a draw object is selected, you will see the borders of the object in the ruler. You can change the borders by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	cy	If the cursor is placed in a table cell, you can change the indents for the contents of the cell by dragging them with the mouse on the ruler. You can change the boundary lines of the table on the ruler or by dragging the actual boundary line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3153750\" src=\"res/helpimg/linleft.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"5.82mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153750\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	cy	These icons mark the left indent for the first line of the current paragraph (top triangle) and the left indent for the other lines of the paragraph (bottom triangle).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3145071\" src=\"res/helpimg/linright.png\" width=\"9.26mm\" height=\"6.61mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	cy	This icon on the right of the ruler marks the right indent of the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	cy	\<emph\>Task\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
