helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	cy	Places the cursor into the previous line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	cy	Down Arrow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	cy	Places the cursor into the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178				0	cy	Enter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	cy	Completes the input in the field and places the cursor into the next field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	cy	As with list boxes or combo boxes, you can open or close the list with a mouse click at the arrow on the right end of the field. However, the input here can be entered either in the opened list or in the top text field. An exception is the properties that expect a list representation, for example, the property \<emph\>List Entries\</emph\>, which can be set for the control fields \<emph\>List Box\</emph\> and \<emph\>Combo Box\</emph\>. Here, you can only edit the entries when the field is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
