helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146950				0	cy	Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344	115			0	cy	An image button has a \<emph\>Graphics \</emph\>property. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_IMAGE_URL\"\>The\<emph\> Graphics\</emph\> property specifies the graphic's path and file name that you want to have displayed on the button.\</ahelp\> If you select the graphic file with the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, the path and file name will be automatically included in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150530				0	cy	Help text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPTEXT\"\>Provides the option of entering a help text that will be displayed as a tip on the control.\</ahelp\> The tip shows the text in user mode when the mouse is moved over the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377				0	cy	Help URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148649				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPURL\"\>Specifies a batch label in URL spelling which refers to a help document and which can be called with the help of the control field.\</ahelp\> The help for the control field help can be opened if the focus is positioned on the control field and the user presses F1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152541				0	cy	Background color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BACKGROUNDCOLOR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the background color of the control field.\</ahelp\>A background color is available for most control fields. If you click on \<emph\>Background color\</emph\>, a list will open which enables you to select among various colors. The "Standard" option adopts the system setting. If the desired color is not listed, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to define a color in the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148971				0	cy	Scrollbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144430				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HSCROLL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.\</ahelp\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110B				0	cy	Incr./decrement value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110F				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines intervals to add or subtract with each activation of the spin box control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146779				0	cy	Value step				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155096	86			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VALUESTEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines spin box intervals.\</ahelp\>You can preset the value intervals in numerical and currency spin boxes. Use the arrow buttons of the spin box to increase or decrease the value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145756				0	cy	List entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRINGITEMLIST\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the list entries visible in the document. Open this list and type your text.\</ahelp\>With list and combo boxes, you can define the list entries that will be visible in the document. Open the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field and type your text. Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"tips\"\>tips \</link\> referring to the entries control and keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152874				0	cy	The predefined default list entry is entered into the \<emph\>Default selection combo\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	cy	Note that the list entries entered here are only incorporated into the form if, on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Content Type\</emph\>, the option "Value List" is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154767				0	cy	If you do not want the list entries to be written to the database or transmitted to the recipient of the Web form, but rather assigned values that are not visible in the form, you can assign the list entries to other values in a value list. The value list is determined on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab. Select the option "Value List" under \<emph\>Type of List Contents\</emph\> and enter the values under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> that are to be assigned to the corresponding visible list entries of the form. For the correct assignment, the order in the value list is relevant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	cy	For HTML documents, a list entry entered on the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab corresponds to the HTML tag <OPTION>; an entry of the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> corresponds to the <OPTION VALUE=...> tag.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	cy	Date max				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148637	122			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149804				0	cy	Max text length				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150776	124			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MAXTEXTLEN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the maximum number of characters that the user can enter.\</ahelp\>For text and combo boxes, you can define the maximum number of characters that the user can enter. If this control field property is uncertain, the default setting will be zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	cy	If the control is linked to a database and the text length is to be accepted from the field definition of the database, you must not enter the text length here. The settings are only accepted from the database if the control property was not defined ("Not Defined" state).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145599				0	cy	Value max				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	126			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines a value for the control field which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields, you can determine the maximum value that the user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154835				0	cy	Time max				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155762	128			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150416				0	cy	Multiselection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MULTISELECTION\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.\</ahelp\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id4040955				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>rich text control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls;rich text control\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148527				0	cy	Text type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153724				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"37933\"\>Allows you to use line breaks and formatting in a control field, such as a text box or label. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key. Select "Multi-line with formatting" to enter formatted text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN113D2				0	cy	If you select the text type "Multi-line with formatting", you cannot bind this control to a database field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11391				0	cy	This control is named "Multiline input" for a text column inside a table control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN114EF				0	cy	Word break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11505				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays text on more than one line.\</ahelp\> Allows you to use line breaks in a text box, so that you can enter more than one line of text. To manually enter a line break, press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11538				0	cy	Toggle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1154E				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies if a Push Button behaves as a Toggle Button. If you set Toggle to "Yes", you can switch between the "selected" and "not selected" control states when you click the button or press the spacebar while the the control has the focus. A button in the "selected" state appears "pressed in".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11558				0	cy	Take Focus on Click				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1156E				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you set this option to "Yes", the Push Button receives the focus when you click the button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11578				0	cy	Hide selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1158E				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"37965\"\>Specifies whether a text selection on a control remains selected when a the focus is no longer on a control.\</ahelp\> If you set \<emph\>Hide selection\</emph\> to "No", the selected text remains selected when the focus is no longer on the control that contains the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11598				0	cy	Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115AE				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"37966\"\>Specifies whether Check boxes and Option buttons are displayed in a 3D look (default) or a flat look.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B8				0	cy	Border color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115CE				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"37967\"\>Specifies the border color for controls that have the Border property set to "flat".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B7				0	cy	Symbol color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115BB				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the color for symbols on controls, for example the arrows on a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149314				0	cy	Date min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755	132			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152866				0	cy	Value min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	134			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can determine here a value for the control field to impede the user to enter a lesser value. That means that a lesser value will not be possible.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields you can determine a minimum value to impede the user to enter a lesser value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153298				0	cy	Time min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	136			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746				0	cy	Decimal accuracy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340				0	cy	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. A name is already entered in the default settings. The control field is specified by its name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	cy	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grouping; controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	cy	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: Controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	cy	Navigation bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426				0	cy	Read-only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which adopts graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	cy	Border				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266				0	cy	Tab order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207				0	cy	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	cy	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	cy	Default status				2002-02-02 02:02:02
