helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148627				0	cy	No				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161673				0	cy	When using the tab key, focusing skips the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159323				0	cy	Yes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	cy	The control can be selected with the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146909				0	cy	Thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154936	148			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SHOWTHOUSANDSEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a thousands separator.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine whether thousands separators are used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256				0	cy	Label				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156432	8			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LABEL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form.\</ahelp\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form. This property determines the visible label or the column header of the data field in table control forms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163820				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>multi-line titles in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159407				0	cy	The \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property is only used for labeling a form element in the interface visible to the user. If you work with macros, note that at runtime, a control is always addressed through the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150293				0	cy	URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147134				0	cy	Currency symbol				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145160	150			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRENCYSYMBOL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a character or a string for the currency symbol.\</ahelp\>In a currency field, you can pre-define the currency symbol by entering the character or string in the \<emph\>Currency symbol\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144444				0	cy	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152417	155			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HIDDEN_VALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter the data that is inherited by the hidden control.\</ahelp\>In a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"hidden control\"\>hidden control\</link\>, under \<emph\>Value\</emph\>, you can enter the data which is inherited by the hidden control. This data will be transferred when sending the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157315				0	cy	Password characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155323	157			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ECHO_CHAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the text box is used as a password input, enter the ASCII-code of the display character. This character is displayed instead of the characters typed by the user for the password.\</ahelp\>If the user enters a password, you can determine the characters that will be displayed instead of the characters typed by the user. Under \<emph\>Password character\</emph\>, enter the ASCII code of the desired character. You can use the values from 0 to 255.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152493				0	cy	The characters corresponding to certain ASCII codes can be seen in the \<emph\>Special Character\</emph\> dialog (Paste - Special Character).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157884				0	cy	Literal mask				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148513				0	cy	The length of the literal mask should always correspond to the length of the edit mask. If this is not the case, the edit mask is either cut off or filled with blanks up to the length of the edit mask.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
