helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	cy	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	cy	Importing and Exporting Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	cy	A left paragraph indent in numbering is indicated as "margin-left" CSS1 property. First-line indents are ignored in numbering and not exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148556				0	cy	Importing and Exporting Spreadsheet Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	cy	$[officename] imports and exports references to deleted sections such as, for example, a referenced column. The whole formula can be viewed during the export process and the deleted reference contains an indication (#REF!) to the reference. A #REF! will be correspondingly created for the reference during the import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150228				0	cy	Importing and Exporting Graphics Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	cy	As with HTML documents, you can choose to use a filter with or without the element ($[officename] Impress) in the name to open a $[officename] graphics file. If without, the file will be opened as a $[officename] Draw document. Otherwise, the file saved by an old program version is now opened in $[officename] Impress.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3144441				0	cy	When you import an EPS file, a preview of the graphic is displayed in the document. If a preview is not available, a placeholder corresponding to the size of the graphic is displayed in the document. Under Unix and Microsoft Windows you can print the imported file by using a PostScript printer. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>If a different printer is used the preview will be printed.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> When exporting EPS graphics, a preview is created and has the TIFF or EPSI format. If an EPS graphic together with other graphics is exported in the EPS format then this file will be embedded unchanged in the new file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	cy	Multipage-TIFFs are allowed when graphics are imported or exported in TIFF format. The graphics are retrieved as a set of individual pictures in a single file, for example, the individual pages of a fax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153213				0	cy	PostScript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	cy	To export a document or graphic in PostScript format:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3163714				0	cy	If you have not yet done so, install a PostScript printer driver, such as the Apple LaserWriter driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	cy	Print the document with the \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3154149				0	cy	Select the PostScript printer in the dialog and mark the \<emph\>Print to file\</emph\> check box. A PostScript file will be created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Context Menu of Web Pages in Read-Only Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158397				0	cy	Context Menu of Web Pages in Read-Only Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_SAVEGRAPHIC\"\>Opens a dialog where you can save the selected graphics.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_COPYLINK\"\>Copies the link at the mouse pointer to the clipboard.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_COPYGRAPHIC\"\>Copies a selected graphic to the clipboard.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	22			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_LOADGRAPHIC\"\>If you have deactivated the graphics display, choose the\<emph\> Load Graphics \</emph\>command to make them visible.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150902				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_GRAPHICOFF\"\>Sets all graphics in the document to be invisible.\</ahelp\> This speeds up the screen display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153910				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MN_READONLY_PLUGINOFF\"\>Disables inserted plug-ins.\</ahelp\> Click this command again to reactivate the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#plugin\" name=\"plug-ins\"\>plug-ins\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
