helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147617				0	cy	Cancel				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155913				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Clicking \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> closes a dialog without saving any changes made.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	cy	Toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783				0	cy	By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414				0	cy	Spin box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	cy	You can type a numerical value into the spin box, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow buttons. On the keyboard you can use the (up-arrow) and (down-arrow) keys to increase or reduce the value in the spin box. You can use (Page up) and (Page down) to set the maximum and minimum value for the spin box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264				0	cy	If the spin box defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232				0	cy	Convert				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you click forward through the dialog, this button is called \<emph\>Next\</emph\>. On the last page the button has the name \<emph\>Convert\</emph\>. The conversion is then performed by clicking the button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129				0	cy	Context Menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553				0	cy	\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename]. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	cy	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements after confirmation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147557				0	cy	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements without requiring confirmation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620				0	cy	Metric				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	cy	You can enter values in the input fields in different units of measurement. The default unit is inches. However, if you want a space of exactly 1cm, then type "1cm". Additional units are available according to the context, for example, 12 pt for a 12 point spacing. If the value of the new unit is unrealistic, the program uses a predefined maximum or minimum value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	cy	Close				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog and saves all changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	cy	Close				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156113				0	cy	Apply				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies the modified or selected values without closing the dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153760				0	cy	Shrink / Maximize				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087	48			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click the\<emph\> Shrink \</emph\>icon to reduce the dialog to the size of the input field. It is then easier to mark the required reference in the sheet. The icons then automatically convert to the \<emph\>Maximize\</emph\> icon. Click it to restore the dialog to its original size.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	cy	The dialog is automatically minimized when you click into a sheet with the mouse. As soon as you release the mouse button, the dialog is restored and the reference range defined with the mouse is highlighted in the document by a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153321				0	cy	Shrink				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	cy	Maximize				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156192				0	cy	Preview Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays a preview of the current selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	cy	Next				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473	71			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click the\<emph\> Next \</emph\>button, and the Wizard uses the current dialog settings and proceeds to the next step. If you are on the last step, this button becomes \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	cy	Back				2002-02-02 02:02:02
