helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000402.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	cy	\<variable id=\"edit3\"\>Choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Open\</emph\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Menu Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156045				0	cy	Menu Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	par_id3150838				0	cy	The window containing the document you want to work on must be selected in order to use the menu commands. Similarly, you must select an object in the document to use the menu commands associated with the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	cy	The menus are context sensitive. This means that those menu items are available that are relevant to the work currently being carried out. If the cursor is located in a text, then all of those menu items are available that are needed to edit the text. If you have selected graphics in a document, then you will see all of the menu items that can be used to edit graphics.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Warning Print Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145759				0	cy	Warning Print Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3152352	2			0	cy	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SD:MODALDIALOG:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS\"\>The\<emph\> Warning Print Options \</emph\>dialog appears when the page setup does not match the defined print range.\</ahelp\> This is the case, for example, if you draw a rectangle that is larger than the current page format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150620				0	cy	Print options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
