helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Special Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>characters; special\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compose key; special characters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	cy	\<variable id=\"insert_specialchar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_specialchar.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Special Characters\"\>Inserting Special Characters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	cy	This function allows you to insert special characters, such as check marks, boxes, and telephone symbols, into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	cy	To view a selection of all characters, choose \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	cy	In the large selection field click the desired character or several characters in succession. The characters are displayed at the bottom of the dialog. When you close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, all displayed characters in the selected font are inserted in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	cy	In any text input field (such as the input fields in the \<emph\>Find&Replace\</emph\> dialog) you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S to call the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630				0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>At present there are three ways of entering letters with accents directly from the keyboard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Sun Solaris:\</emph\> Using a Sun keyboard. First press the Compose key to the right of the space bar, then enter the first and second modifiers. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Linux / NetBSD:\</emph\> Using the dead-keys. In an xterm window first press the (´) or (`) key. The character should not appear on the screen. Now press a letter, such as "e". The e is given an accent, é or è. If not, then check in the XF86Config file if a "nodeadkeys" XkbdVariant has been loaded there and replace it. You may also have set the environment variable SAL_NO_DEADKEYS, which deactivates the dead-keys. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>All Unix systems:\</emph\> (Alt Graph) as additional compose key. The (Alt Graph) key can work in $[officename] like the Compose key, if you set the environment variable SAL_ALTGR_COMPOSE. The (Alt Graph) key must trigger a mode_switch, so, for example, xmodmap -e "keysym Alt_R = Mode_switch" must be set. First press (Alt Graph), then the first modifier, then the second modifier. The characters are combined as described on a Solaris system in the file /usr/openwin/include/X11/Suncompose.h. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special Characters\"\>Special Characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect\"\>AutoCorrect\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Opening Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>opening; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; opening documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; creating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; new\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	cy	\<variable id=\"doc_open\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_open.xhp\" name=\"Opening Documents\"\>Opening Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	cy	Opening an existing document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	cy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	cy	Click the Open File icon				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	cy	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	cy	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	cy	Restrict Files to Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	cy	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	cy	Opening an Empty Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	cy	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	cy	You can also enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog. This must start with the fully extended form with file:/// or ftp:// or http://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	cy	When you open a file by an URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens the remote file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	cy	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	cy	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	cy	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	cy	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	cy	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	cy	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	cy	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	cy	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	cy	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - E-mail\</emph\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	cy	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Changing the Title of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	cy	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	cy	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	cy	How to change the title of the current document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	cy	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	cy	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;from XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing; XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>testing;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing/distributing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	cy	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	cy	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	cy	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	cy	\<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	cy	\<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	cy	\<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	cy	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	cy	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	cy	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	cy	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	cy	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	cy	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	cy	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	cy	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	cy	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	cy	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	cy	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	cy	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	cy	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognizing URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; turning off recognition of addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	cy	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	cy	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognizes a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (color and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	cy	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognize URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	cy	Undo URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	cy	When you are typing and notice that a text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	cy	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350				0	cy	Turn off URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	cy	Load a document of the type for which you want to modify the URL recognition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	cy	If you want to modify the URL recognition for text documents, open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	cy	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	cy	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	cy	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Executing SQL Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing commands\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;creating in SQL view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>commands;SQL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>executing;SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	cy	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	cy	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	cy	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	cy	To execute an SQL statement directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	cy	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbanativesql.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	98			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> or \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153159\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153159\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to save the query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	cy	If you are using Microsoft Windows, you can manage your certificates from the Control Panel applet "Internet Options" on the "Contents" tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	cy	If you are using Solaris or Linux, you must install a recent version of Thunderbird, Mozilla Suite, or Firefox software to install some system files that are needed for encryption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10720				0	cy	If you have created different profiles in Thunderbird, Mozilla, or Firefox, and you want %PRODUCTNAME to use one specified profile for certificates, then you can set the environment variable MOZILLA_CERTIFICATE_FOLDER to point to the folder of that specified profile.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	cy	Signing a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Digital Signatures\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10690				0	cy	A message box advises you to save the document. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to save the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	cy	After saving, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/digitalsignatures.xhp\"\>Digital Signatures\</link\> dialog. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to add a public key to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	cy	In the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/selectcertificate.xhp\"\>Select Certificate\</link\> dialog, select your certificate and click OK. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	cy	You see again the Digital Signatures dialog, where you can add more certificates if you want. Click OK to add the public key to the saved file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	cy	Signing the macros inside a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	cy	Normally, macros are part of a document. If you sign a document, the macros inside the document are signed automatically. If you want to sign only the macros, but not the document, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Digital Signature\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	cy	Apply the signature as described above for documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>readers;accessibility\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input devices for disabled persons\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	cy	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	cy	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	cy	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	cy	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	cy	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	cy	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	cy	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	cy	Supported Assistive Tools				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	cy	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	cy	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	cy	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	cy	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	cy	Supported Input Devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	cy	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	cy	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	cy	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	cy	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	cy	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149180				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>page formats; maximizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; maximizing page formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; maximum page formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	cy	\<variable id=\"pageformat_max\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pageformat_max.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\"\>Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	cy	Not all printers can print a paper up to its edges. Most of them leave an unprinted margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	cy	$[officename] offers a semi-automatic feature that enables you to print as close to the paper's edge as is possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	cy	Make sure that your printer has been setup under \<emph\>File - Printer Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	cy	Make sure that the \<emph\>Online Layout\</emph\> in the \<emph\>View\</emph\> menu is not selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	cy	Select the \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> command, and go to the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	cy	Under \<emph\>Margins\</emph\> you can define the maximum or minimum possible value for the page margins (left, right, top, and bottom). Click into the respective spin box, then press the (Page Up) or (Page Down) key. The preview displays a dashed line around the printable range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
