helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A61				0	cy	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A65				0	cy	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A69				0	cy	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A71				0	cy	Click the option button for %PRODUCTNAME or Writer (or whichever application is currently open). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A74				0	cy	Selecting the option button sets the scope of the new key combination to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
