helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master passwords\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>form control protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in text;protecting cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	cy	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	cy	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	cy	Protecting All Documents When Saving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	cy	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"XML format\"\>XML format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	cy	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	cy	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	cy	Protecting Revision Marking				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	cy	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	cy	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	cy	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	cy	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	cy	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	cy	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	cy	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	cy	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	cy	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	cy	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	cy	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	cy	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	cy	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	cy	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	cy	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	cy	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	cy	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Changing Your Work Directory				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>work directory change\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>My Documents folder; work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; changing paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;work directory\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	cy	\<variable id=\"workfolder\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/workfolder.xhp\" name=\"Changing Your Work Directory\"\>Changing Your Work Directory\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	cy	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your work directory. To change this directory:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	cy	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the\<emph\> Edit button, or \</emph\>double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the work directory you want and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Paths\"\>Paths\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	cy	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	cy	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	cy	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"http://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>http://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	cy	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	cy	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	cy	To create an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	cy	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	cy	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	cy	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	cy	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	cy	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	cy	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	cy	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	cy	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	cy	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	cy	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	cy	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	cy	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	cy	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	cy	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	cy	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	cy	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	cy	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	cy	To test an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	cy	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	cy	The document is not altered by these tests. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	cy	Create or open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	cy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	cy	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Text XSLTs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	cy	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	cy	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	cy	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	cy	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Printing with Reduced Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	bm_id5201574				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>gradients;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resolution when printing bitmaps \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reduced printing;faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>speed of printing;faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing speed\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;transparencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;faster\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faster printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	cy	\<variable id=\"print_faster\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_faster.xhp\"\>Printing faster with Reduced Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	cy	You can decide to reduce the data necessary to print your document. The settings can be defined differently for printing directly to the printer or for printing to a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	cy	Click one of the following settings options: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	cy	\<emph\>Printer\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>to define options for reducing data while printing directly to a printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	cy	\<emph\>Print to file\</emph\>\<emph\>-\</emph\> to define options for reducing data while printing to a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	cy	Select any combination of the four options, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	cy	All documents that you print from now on will use the changed options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	cy	Print your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	cy	You can reduce data for transparency, for gradients, or for bitmaps. When you reduce the data, on many printers you will not see a reduction of printing quality. But the printing time is substantially shorter, and when you print to a file, the file size is much smaller.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>Print options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
