helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	cy	\<variable id=\"ms_user\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_user.xhp\" name=\"Using Microsoft Office and $[officename]\"\>Using Microsoft Office and $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	cy	$[officename] can open and save documents in the Microsoft Office file formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	cy	Opening a Microsoft Office File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>. Select a Microsoft Office file in the $[officename] file open dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	cy	MS Office file...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	cy	...will open in $[officename] module				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	cy	MS Word, *.doc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	cy	$[officename] Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898				0	cy	MS Excel, *.xls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	cy	$[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147574				0	cy	MS PowerPoint, *.ppt, *.pps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	cy	$[officename] Impress				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	cy	Saving as a Microsoft Office File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	cy	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box, select a Microsoft Office file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	cy	Saving Documents by Default in Microsoft Office Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3148453				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Standard file format\</emph\> area, first select a document type, then select the file type for saving.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807	18			0	cy	From now on, if you save a document, the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>will be set according to your choice. Of course, you still can select another file type in the file save dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	cy	Opening Microsoft Office Files by Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153092				0	cy	Converting Many Microsoft Office Files into OpenDocument Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	cy	The \<emph\>Document Converter Wizard\</emph\> will copy and convert all Microsoft Office files in a folder into $[officename] documents in the OpenDocument file format. You can specify the folder to be read, and the folder where the converted files are to be saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	cy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\> to start the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154319				0	cy	Macros in Microsoft Office and $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921				0	cy	Microsoft Office and $[officename] cannot run the same macro code. Microsoft Office uses VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code, and $[officename] uses Basic code based on the $[officename] API (Application Program Interface) environment. Although the programming language is the same, the objects and methods are different.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	cy	If you use macros in one of the applications and want to use the same functionality in the other application, you must edit the macros. $[officename] can load the macros that are contained within Microsoft Office files and you can then view and edit the macro code in the $[officename] \<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Basic IDE\"\>Basic IDE\</link\> editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	cy	You can choose to preserve or delete VBA macros				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	cy	Open a Microsoft Office document that contains VBA macro code. Change only the normal contents (text, cells, graphics), and do not edit the macros. Save the document as a Microsoft Office file type. Open the file in Microsoft Office, and the VBA macros will run as before.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	cy	You may delete the VBA macros from the Microsoft Office file on loading or on saving.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Drawing Lines in Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143206				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>arrows; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indicator lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; removing automatic lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing;lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic lines/borders in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143206				0	cy	\<variable id=\"line_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Lines in Text\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	cy	You can incorporate lines into your text with custom angles, width, color, and other attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	cy	To define the line attributes and direction, use the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> drawing object as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3166410\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertdraw.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3166410\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3154285\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154285\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	cy	1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	41			0	cy	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Show Draw Functions \</emph\>icon to open the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon. The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol with a line beside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117				0	cy	2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	cy	In your document, click where the line should begin. Hold down the mouse button and drag to the point where you want the line to end. If you also hold down the Shift key, you can draw only horizontal, vertical, and diagonal lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	cy	3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	43			0	cy	Release the mouse button once the line has the desired direction and length. You can then draw more lines. End this function by pressing the Esc key or by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon from the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	cy	4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	cy	After clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon, you can select all of the lines at the same time by clicking each line while holding down the Shift key. This multiple selection enables you to assign all of them a common color, width or other attribute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	cy	Create a horizontal line by applying the preset Paragraph Style \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\>. Click into an empty paragraph, and double-click the \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\> Style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. If the entry for horizontal lines is not visible in the list of Paragraph Styles, select "All Styles" in the lower listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	cy	You can draw a line above, beside or below a paragraph by choosing \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	cy	Automatic lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	cy	If you start a new line by typing some consecutive hyphen or underline characters and press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key, the characters are removed and the previous paragraph gets a line as a bottom border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D0				0	cy	To remove an automatically drawn border, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Border\</emph\> and select no border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	cy	To undo an automatic border replacement once, choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E0				0	cy	To disable the automatic borders, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Options\</emph\> and clear \<emph\>Apply border\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	cy	The lines and other drawing objects that you insert in text are not defined in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>, and are therefore not exported directly into HTML format. Instead, they are exported as graphics.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting and Editing Tab Stops				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144436				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default tab stops in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;tab stops on ruler\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	cy	\<variable id=\"tabs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/tabs.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\"\>Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id1376079				0	cy	On the horizontal ruler you can see the tab stops for the current paragraph. If you want to change the tab stops, you should first consider the scope to which you want to change tab stops as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id274971				0	cy	Change the tab stops for all paragraphs using the current Paragraph Style: Right-click the paragraph to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id5199133				0	cy	Change the tab stops for one or more paragraphs: Select the paragraphs, then click inside the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id6178167				0	cy	In the following, you find instructions for all above mentioned tasks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	27			0	cy	You can set a tab stop by clicking on the ruler or by selecting \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Tabs.\</emph\> Both methods affect the current paragraph or all selected paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	cy	Click the ruler once to set a left-justified tab. Right-click a tab icon on the ruler to see the context menu in which you can change the tab type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	cy	To set several decimal tabs one after the other, keep clicking the icon to the left of the ruler until the desired tab type is shown, then click on the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
