helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	cy	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	cy	Inserting Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	cy	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	cy	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	cy	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	cy	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	cy	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	cy	Editing Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	cy	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	cy	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	cy	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	cy	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	cy	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Image, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	cy	Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	cy	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image. This is only possible in $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	cy	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	cy	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	cy	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	cy	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	cy	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	cy	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	cy	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	cy	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	cy	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	cy	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	cy	Select one of the options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	cy	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	cy	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	cy	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	cy	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	cy	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	cy	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	cy	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Relative and Absolute Links				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>absolute hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks, see also links\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	cy	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_rel_abs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp\" name=\"Relative and Absolute Links\"\>Relative and Absolute Links\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	cy	When you include hyperlinks, two factors must be taken into account: whether they are set as relative or absolute on saving, and whether or not the file is present.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	cy	An absolute path such as "C:\\homepage\\graphics\\picture.gif" would no longer function on the provider server. Neither a server nor the computer of a reader needs to have a C hard drive: operating systems such as Unix or MacOS do not recognize drive letters, and even if the folder homepage\\graphics existed, your picture would not be available. It is better to use relative addressing for file links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	cy	A link to a web page, for example, "www.sun.com" or "www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.htm" is an absolute link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	cy	$[officename] also reacts differently, depending on whether the file referred to in the link exists, and where it is located. $[officename] checks every new link and sets a target and protocol automatically. The result can be seen in the generated HTML code after saving the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145317				0	cy	The following rules apply: A relative reference ("graphic/picture.gif") is only possible when both files exist on the same drive. If the files are on different drives in your local file system, the absolute reference follows the "file:" protocol ("file:///data1/xyz/picture.gif"). If the files are on different servers or if the target of the link is not available, the absolute reference uses the "http:" protocol ("http://data2/abc/picture.gif").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	cy	Be sure to organize all files for your homepage on the same drive as the start file of the homepage. In this way, $[officename] can set the protocol and target so that the reference on the server is always correct.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	cy	When you rest your mouse on a hyperlink, a help tip displays the absolute reference, since $[officename] uses absolute path names internally. The complete path and address can only be seen when you view the result of the HTML export, by loading the HTML file as "Text" or opening it with a text editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Searching Tables and Form Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id4066896				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>finding;records in form documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;finding records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;tables and forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	cy	\<variable id=\"data_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching Tables and Form Documents\"\>Searching Tables and Form Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	cy	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	cy	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	cy	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	cy	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	cy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	cy	Designing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	cy	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	cy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	cy	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	cy	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	cy	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	cy	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	cy	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	cy	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
