helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147143				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>mobile devices filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pocket device appliances\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;mobile devices filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Palm file filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Pocket PC file filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;documents for mobile devices\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;mobile device documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;Pocket PC formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;Pocket PC and $[officename] formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;mobile devices filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147143				0	cy	\<variable id=\"mobiledevicefilters\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/mobiledevicefilters.xhp\" name=\"Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\"\>Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	cy	You can save and open documents to and from several mobile devices file formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	cy	Currently the following filters are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	cy	AportisDoc for Palm OS compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	cy	Pocket Excel for Pocket PC compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	cy	Pocket Word for Pocket PC compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	cy	Installing the Pocket PC filters under Windows will also install a DLL file that supports the synchronize software of your Pocket PC.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	cy	The Java Runtime Environment is required to use the mobile device filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665				0	cy	Installing the mobile devices filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	cy	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	cy	If you are using the Windows opearating system with ActiveSync installed, disconnect any Pocket PC device from ActiveSync.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	cy	Start the $[officename] Setup program:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	cy	Open the Windows \<emph\>Start\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>, double-click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION entry, click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	cy	In Setup, choose the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	cy	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry, then open the \<emph\>Mobile Device Filters\</emph\> entry. Select the filters you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Install\</emph\>, \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to install the filters and exit the Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123				0	cy	Saving $[officename] documents for a mobile device				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	cy	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	cy	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	cy	Opening mobile device documents in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	cy	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	cy	Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159196				0	cy	Synchronizing file types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	cy	To convert Pocket PC formats to and from $[officename] formats, you must first change some options within ActiveSync. To do this, open the ActiveSync window and open its Options dialog. Perform the following steps:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	cy	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Conversion Settings\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Device to Desktop\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Pocket Word Document - Pocket PC\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	29			0	cy	In the drop down list of available conversions, select \<emph\>$[officename] Writer \</emph\>and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	cy	Repeat steps 4 and 5 for \<emph\>Pocket Excel Workbook\</emph\> selecting \<emph\>$[officename] Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	cy	After these steps you can copy documents between $[officename] and your Pocket PC, either by the ActiveSync software or by the Windows Explorer. The filters will be applied to the document files automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	cy	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	cy	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	cy	Select the drawing object or objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	cy	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	cy	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	cy	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	cy	Inserting into a text document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	cy	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	cy	Inserting into a spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	cy	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156410				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>start parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command line parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;command line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arguments in command line\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410				0	cy	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	cy	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	cy	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	cy	Starting the $[officename] Software From the Command Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	cy	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	cy	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open \</emph\>text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	cy	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	cy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	cy	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	cy	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	cy	Valid Command Line Parameters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
