helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	cy	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	cy	Open your original document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	cy	A file selection dialog appears. Select the copy of the document and confirm the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	cy	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into your original document. All text passages that occur in your document but not in the copy are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that are missing in your original document are identified as deletions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	cy	You can now accept the "insertions", in which case the relevant texts stay in their original form, or you can accept the "deletions", in which case the marked text contained in the copy is not inserted in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
