helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	cy	Please note that accessibility support relies on Sun Microsystems Java technology for communications with assistive technology tools. This means that the first program startup may take a few seconds longer, because the Java runtime environment has to be started as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Recording Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;recording changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	cy	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	cy	The review function is available in $[officename] for text documents and spreadsheet documents. Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	cy	1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	cy	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	cy	2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	cy	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	cy	3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	cy	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119				0	cy	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	cy	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	cy	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	cy	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Version Management				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>versions; of a document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; version management\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>version management\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	cy	\<variable id=\"redlining_versions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_versions.xhp\" name=\"Version Management\"\>Version Management\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	cy	The \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu contains a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01190000.xhp\" name=\"Versions\"\>\<emph\>Versions\</emph\>\</link\> command that enables you to save multiple versions of a document in the same file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149399				0	cy	You can choose to view individual versions of a document, or you can display the differences between versions with color markings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	cy	In the dialog to open a document, you can select from a combo box which version of this document you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	cy	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	cy	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	cy	Installing the ActiveX control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	cy	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	cy	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	cy	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	cy	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	cy	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	cy	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	cy	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	cy	Viewing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	cy	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	cy	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	cy	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	cy	Editing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	cy	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	cy	Edit the copy of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Recording a Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	bm_id3093440				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>macros; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; macros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic; recording macros\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id3093440				0	cy	\<variable id=\"macro_recording\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/macro_recording.xhp\" name=\"Recording a Macro\"\>Recording a Macro\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	cy	Open the document for which you want to record a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Record Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	cy	You see the small \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog with just one button called \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	cy	Perform the actions you want to be recorded in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	cy	Press the Escape key to deselect an object, as the macro recorder currently does not record this action by mouse click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	cy	The \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you can save and run the macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	cy	If you want to abort the recording without saving a macro, click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button of the \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	cy	To save the macro, first select the object where you want the macro to be saved in the \<emph\>Save macro in\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	12			0	cy	If you want the macro to be saved into a new library or module, click the \<emph\>New Library \</emph\>or \<emph\>New Module \</emph\>button and enter a name for the library or module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	cy	Enter a name for the new macro in the \<emph\>Macro name\</emph\> text box. Do not use Basic keywords as a name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"macro programming in $[officename]\"\>Programming in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id7797242				0	cy	The macro recording functionality is only available for text documents in %PRODUCTNAME Writer and for spreadsheets in %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using and Editing Database Reports 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;opening and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
