helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	cy	Using a Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	cy	%PRODUCTNAME stores the templates for reports in a database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file that you want to create the report for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	cy	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	cy	Double-click one of the report links to open the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	cy	These links are added automatically by the Report Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104				0	cy	Editing a Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	cy	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialog page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialog page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	cy	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	cy	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Copying Graphics Between Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	cy	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	cy	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	cy	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	cy	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	cy	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	cy	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	cy	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	cy	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	cy	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	cy	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	cy	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	cy	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	cy	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	cy	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	cy	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	cy	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	cy	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	cy	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	cy	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	cy	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	cy	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
