helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	cy	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	cy	Open a form document that contains database fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	cy	On the \<emph\>Form Object\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	cy	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	cy	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	cy	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	cy	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	cy	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using Digital Signatures				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>signing documents;digital signatures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>certificates;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;using\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	cy	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can digitally sign your documents and macros. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	cy	To sign a document digitally, you need a personal key, the certificate. A personal key is stored on your computer as a combination of a private key, which must be kept secret, and a public key, which you add to your documents when you sign them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	cy	Save and sign the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	cy	When you apply a digital signature to a document, a kind of checksum is computed from the document's content plus your personal key. The checksum and your public key are stored together with the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	cy	Open a signed document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	cy	When someone later opens the document on any computer with a recent version of %PRODUCTNAME, the program will compute the checksum again and compare it with the stored checksum. If both are the same, the program will signal that you see the original, unchanged document. In addition, the program can show you the public key information from the certificate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	cy	You can compare the public key with the public key that is published on the web site of the certificate authority.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	cy	Whenever someone changes something in the document, this change breaks the digital signature. After the change, there will be no sign that you see the original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Using Context Menus				2002-02-02 02:02:02
