helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	cy	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Create Form in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	cy	A new text document opens. Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls\</link\> to insert form controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10670				0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon to access all forms that were created from within the current database window. In addition, you can use the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> icons to add database form controls to any Writer or Calc document, but these documents will not be listed in the database window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Printing Address Labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>creating;address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	cy	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	cy	Select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. Remember to mark \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	cy	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	cy	When you see the label document, open the data source view by choosing \<emph\>View - Data Sources\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	cy	You can then save and/or print the label document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>protected spaces;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces; inserting protected spaces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphens; as separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separators; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dashes;replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-breaking dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected dashes;inserting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	cy	\<variable id=\"space_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/space_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\"\>Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	cy	Non-breaking spaces				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	cy	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you type a space between the words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	cy	Non-breaking dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	cy	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	cy	Hyphen, dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	cy	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option. This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with a long dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	cy	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	cy	Definite separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	cy	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	$[officename] HTML Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/07/09000000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] HTML Templates\"\>$[officename] HTML Templates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	cy	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	cy	A tool for creating new web pages is the Online-Layout-Mode, which you can open by choosing \<emph\>View - Online Layout\</emph\>. As soon as you have activated this mode you will see only those options in the menus and dialogs of $[officename] which can be used on HTML pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	cy	Creating a New Web Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	cy	Switch to the online layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Online Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document. $[officename] will then internally use the html.stw template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	cy	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types, such as the .HTM or .HTML extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
