helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055D				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Tools menu of a database window.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	cy	Relationships				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN10576				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020000.xhp\"\>Relation Design\</link\> view and checks whether the database connection supports relations.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058A				0	cy	User Administration				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058E				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the User Administration dialog if the database supports this feature.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	cy	Table Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_TABLE_SELECTOR\"\>Opens the Table Filter dialog where you can specify which tables of the database to show or to hide.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	cy	Select the tables that you want to filter in the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	cy	If you select the topmost table in a hierarchy, all of the tables in the hierarchy are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	cy	If you select a table that is at a lower level in the hierarchy, the tables that occur above it in the hierarchy are not selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BC				0	cy	SQL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menutools.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C0				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the SQL dialog where you can enter SQL statements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Forms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150476				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04000000.xhp\" name=\"Forms\"\>Forms\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156136				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>forms; general information\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	cy	Forms can be used to enter or to edit existing database contents easily.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157910				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\" name=\"Form Wizard\"\>FormWizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156003				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Form Controls\"\>Form Controls\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	cy	The Form Controls toolbar offers the tools required to create a form in a text, table, drawing, or presentation document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155388				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Form in Design Mode\"\>Form in Design Mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	cy	In design mode, the form is designed and the properties of the form and the controls contained in it are defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149784				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Sorting and Filtering Data\"\>Sorting and Filtering Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\04000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	cy	You will find the sorting and filter functions in the toolbar when you open a form in user mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	JDBC Connection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10600				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the options to access a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#jdbc\" name=\"JDBC\"\>JDBC\</link\> database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10623				0	cy	JDBC Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10627				0	cy	\<item type=\"productname\"\>You can use a JDBC driver class to connect to a JDBC database from %PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. The driver class is provided by the database manufacturer. Two examples of JDBC databases are Oracle and MySQL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	cy	Oracle database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10638				0	cy	You can use a JDBC driver to access an Oracle database from Solaris or Linux. To access the database from Windows, you need an ODBC driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064B				0	cy	On UNIX, ensure that the Oracle database client is installed with JDBC support. The JDBC driver class for the Solaris Oracle client version 8.x is located in the <Oracle client>/product/jdbc/lib/classes111.zip directory. You can also download the latest version of the version from the Oracle web site:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064E				0	cy	http://otn.oracle.com/tech/java/sqlj_jdbc/content.html				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> box, enter the location of the Oracle database server. The syntax of the URL depends on the database type. See the documentation that came with the JDBC driver for more information. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10668				0	cy	For an Oracle database, the syntax of the URL is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	cy	oracle:thin:@hostname:port:database_name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	cy	hostname is the name of the machine that runs the Oracle database. You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	cy	port is the port where the Oracle database listens. Ask your database administrator for the correct port address.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	cy	database_name is the name of the Oracle database. Ask your database administrator for the correct name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	cy	MySQL database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	cy	The mm.mysql-2.0.4-bin.jar driver archive for the MySQL database is available on the following web site:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10689				0	cy	The syntax for a MySQL database is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	cy	mysql://hostname:port/database_name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10695				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>hostname is the name of the machine that runs the MySQL database.\</ahelp\> You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	cy	port is the default port for MySQL databases, namely 3306.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	cy	database_name is the name of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	cy	Data source URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_CONNURL_JDBCPAGE\"\>Enter the URL for the database. For example, for the MySQL JDBC driver, enter "jdbc:mysql://<Servername>/<name of the database>". For more information on the JDBC driver, consult the documentation that came with the driver.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
