helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\" name=\"Connectors\"\>Connectors\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	cy	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_connector.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	cy	Connector				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConnectorToolbox\"\>Open the \<emph\>Connectors\</emph\> toolbar, where you can add connectors to objects in the current slide. A connector is a line that joins objects, and remains attached when the objects are moved. If you copy an object with a connector, the connector is also copied.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	cy	There are four types of connector lines:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145584				0	cy	Standard (90-degree angle bends)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154485				0	cy	Line (two bends)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153817				0	cy	Straight				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	cy	Curved				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148604				0	cy	When you click a connector and move your mouse pointer over a filled object, or the edge of an unfilled object, connection points appear. A connection point is a fixed point where you can attach a connector line. If you want, you can add a custom connection point, called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10030200.xhp\" name=\"glue point\"\>glue point\</link\>, to an object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	cy	To draw a connector line, click a connection point on an object, drag to a connection point on another object, and then release. You can also drag to an empty part of you document and click. The unattached end of the connector is locked in place, until you drag the end to a different location. To detach a connector, drag either end of the connector line to a different location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147297				0	cy	Connector				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166468				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Connector\"\>Draws a connector with one or more 90-degree angle bends. Click a connection point on an object, drag to a connection point on another object, and then release.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
