helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	15			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>area, set the options for the layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The new layer automatically becomes the active layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	cy	To change the properties of a layer, click the name tab of the layer, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153814				0	cy	You cannot change the name of or delete a predefined \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	cy	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	cy	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	cy	To convert text into a drawing object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	cy	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	cy	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	cy	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	cy	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	cy	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Changing the Slide Background Fill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150199				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides;changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	33			0	cy	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Background Fill\"\>Changing the Slide Background Fill\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	cy	You can change the background color or the background fill of the current slide or all of the slides in your document. For a background fill, you can use hatching, a gradient, or a bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	cy	If you want to change the background fill for all of the slides, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. To change the background fill of a single slide, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	cy	To use a color, gradient, or hatching pattern for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149942				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148725	51			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, and then click a color in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\>, and then click a gradient style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\>, and then click a hatching style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244				0	cy	To use an image for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	cy	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	cy	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	cy	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	cy	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403				0	cy	This modification is only valid for the current presentation document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	cy	To save a new slide master as a template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\> to change the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> to change the slide background, or choose other formatting commands. Add objects that will be visible on all slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to close the master view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> to save the document as a template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10847				0	cy	Enter a name for the template. Do not change the category from "My Templates". Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	cy	Now you can use the Presentation Wizard to open a new presentation based on your new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
