helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id2901394				0	cy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5674611				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1308023				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Handouts\</emph\> and click OK on both dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	cy	Printing a range of slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	cy	Hold down Shift, and click the range of slides that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	cy	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Print range \</emph\>area, click \<emph\>Pages\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561				0	cy	When the numbers of the selected slides appear in the \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> box, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Creating Animated GIF Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	cy	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	cy	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	cy	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	cy	To create an animated GIF:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	cy	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	cy	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	cy	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	cy	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	cy	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	cy	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	cy	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	cy	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	cy	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	cy	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	About Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	cy	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	cy	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	cy	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	cy	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	cy	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	cy	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	cy	Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	cy	Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	cy	Dimension Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	cy	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	cy	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	cy	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	cy	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	cy	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Selecting Underlying Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
