helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	cy	Up to four colors can be replaced at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	cy	You can also use the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> option to replace the transparent areas of an image with a color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	cy	Ensure that the image you are using is a bitmap (for example, BMP, GIF, JPG, or PNG) or a metafile (for example, WMF).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	cy	Click the color in the image. The color appears in the first \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> box and the check box next to the color is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	cy	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, select the new color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	cy	This replaces all occurrences of the \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	cy	If you want to replace another color while the dialog is open, select the check box in front of \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the next row and repeat steps 3 to 5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
