helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166392				0	cy	\<emph\>Data_Y\</emph\> represents the Y Data array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166411				0	cy	\<emph\>Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the X Data array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173797				0	cy	\<emph\>New_Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the X data array, in which the values are recalculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173817				0	cy	\<emph\>Function_Type\</emph\>(optional). If Function_Type = 0, functions in the form y = m^x will be calculated. Otherwise, y = b*m^x functions will be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3173839				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173852				0	cy	This function returns an array and is handled in the same way as the other array functions. Select a range where you want the answers to appear and select the function. Select Data_Y. Enter any other parameters, mark \<emph\>Array\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
