helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153122				0	cy	In this page you can view the structure of the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149350				0	cy	If you start \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> while the cell cursor is positioned in a cell that already contains a function, the \<emph\>Structure\</emph\> tab is opened and shows the composition of the current formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149014				0	cy	Structure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150481				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_STRUCT\"\>Displays a hierarchical representation of the current function.\</ahelp\> You can hide or show the arguments by a click on the plus or minus sign in front.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886				0	cy	Blue dots denote correctly entered arguments. Red dots indicate incorrect data types. For example: if the SUM function has one argument entered as text, this is highlighted in red as SUM only permits number entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	MONTH 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149936				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>MONTH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149936				0	cy	\<variable id=\"month\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_month.xhp\"\>MONTH\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3153538				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MONAT\"\>Returns the month for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The month is returned as an integer between 1 and 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149517				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	cy	MONTH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal for which the month is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153322				0	cy	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3149244				0	cy	MONTH(NOW()) returns the current month				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3154790				0	cy	MONTH(C4) returns 7 if contents of C4 = 7/7/00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Fill Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
