helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\format_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id2480544				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Switches \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> mode for an inserted freeform line on and off.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Trace Dependents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing dependents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030300.xhp\" name=\"Trace Dependents\"\>Trace Dependents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowDependents\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Draws tracer arrows to the active cell from formulas that depend on values in the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	cy	The area of all cells that are used together with the active cell in a formula is highlighted by a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	cy	This function works per level. For instance, if one level of traces has already been activated to show the precedents (or dependents), then you would see the next dependency level by activating the \<emph\>Trace\</emph\> function again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Protect Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Protect Document\"\>Protect Document\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362	2			0	cy	The\<emph\> Protect Document \</emph\>command prevents changes from being made to cells in the sheets or to sheets in a document. As an option, you can define a password. If a password is defined, removal of the protection is only possible if the user enters the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147228				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060100.xhp\" name=\"Sheets\"\>Sheets\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060200.xhp\" name=\"Documents\"\>Documents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159399				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>syllables in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	cy	Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	2			0	cy	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Hyphenate\"\>The \<emph\>Hyphenation \</emph\>command calls the dialog for setting the hyphenation in $[officename] Calc.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	cy	You can only turn on the automatic hyphenation in $[officename] Calc when the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\" name=\"row break\"\>row break\</link\> feature is active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153192				0	cy	Hyphenation for selected cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
