helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	cy	e, h, k, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146125				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3153695				0	cy	CONVERT_ADD(Number;From unit;To unit)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3147522	211			0	cy	Number: the number to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472	212			0	cy	From unit: the unit from which conversion is taking place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790	213			0	cy	To unit: the unit to which conversion is taking place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156270				0	cy	Examples:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3156336	215			0	cy	=CONVERT_ADD(10;"HP";"PS") returns, rounded to two decimal places, 10.14. 10 HP equal 10.14 PS.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154834	216			0	cy	=CONVERT_ADD(10;"km";"mi")returns, rounded to two decimal places, 6.21. 10 Kilometers equal 6.21 miles. The k is the permitted prefix character for the factor 10^3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147096				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>FACTDOUBLE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147096				0	cy	FACTDOUBLE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3151309				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FACTDOUBLE\"\>The result is the factorial of the number with increments of 2.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154666				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3155121				0	cy	FACTDOUBLE(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3158440	40			0	cy	Number: if the number is even, the following factorial is calculated: n*(N-2)*(n-4)*...*4*2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154622				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060116.xhp	0	help	par_id3154116	43			0	cy	=FACTDOUBLE(6) returns 48.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
