helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	2			0	cy	\<variable id=\"addintext\"\>The following describes and lists the available add-in functions. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp#addinconcept\"\>Add-in concept\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	5			0	cy	You will also find a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\"\>description of the $[officename] Calc add-in interface\</link\> in the Help. In addition, important functions and their parameters are described in the Help for the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>$[officename] Calc add-in DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	cy	Add-ins supplied				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	cy	$[officename] contains examples for the add-in interface of $[officename] Calc. These provide the functions that you find in \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> (choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>) under the \<emph\>Add-in\</emph\> category, plus several of the financial functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
