helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145358				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	cy	DAYSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153803				0	cy	Date: The date up through which a number of days in the year is calculated. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153487				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	cy	DAYSINYEAR(A1) returns 366 days if A1 contains 2/29/68, a valid date for the year 1968.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
