helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145237				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145237				0	cy	WEEKSINYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_WEEKSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of weeks in a year until a certain date.\</ahelp\> The number of weeks is defined as follows: a week that spans two years is added to the year in which most days of that week occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149719				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145638				0	cy	WEEKSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	cy	Date: The date until which the weeks in the year will be calculated. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147614				0	cy	WEEKSINYEAR(A1) returns 53 if A1 contains 2/17/70, a valid date for the year 1970.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
