helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518				0	cy	CEILING				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454				0	cy	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467				0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000				0	cy	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020				0	cy	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is given and not equal to zero, and if \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	cy	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	cy	=CEILING( -11; -2) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	cy	=CEILING( -11; -2; 0) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	cy	=CEILING( -11; -2; 1) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
