helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822				0	cy	PI()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370				0	cy	Pi is 3.14159... as a rounded value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418				0	cy	MULTINOMIAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660				0	cy	MULTINOMIAL (Number(s))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673				0	cy	Number(s): a list of up to 30 numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701				0	cy	=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11) returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values 2, 3 and 4. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717				0	cy	POWER				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns the result of a number raised to a power.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159526				0	cy	POWER(base; power) or base ^ power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540				0	cy	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> is the number that is to be raised to a given power.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594				0	cy	If you enter 3 as the base and -2 as the power, 0.11 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651				0	cy	SERIESSUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708				0	cy	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	cy	SERIESSUM(x; n; m; coefficients)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737				0	cy	x: the number as an independent variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344				0	cy	n: the starting power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357				0	cy	m: the increment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370				0	cy	coefficients: a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386				0	cy	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	cy	PRODUCT(number 1 to 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460				0	cy	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494				0	cy	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 24 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340				0	cy	SUMSQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totaling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402				0	cy	SUMSQ(number 1 to 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415				0	cy	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449				0	cy	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the \<emph\>Number 1\</emph\>; \<emph\>2\</emph\> and \<emph\>3\</emph\> text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247				0	cy	MOD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder after a number is divided by a divisor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308				0	cy	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321				0	cy	\<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is the value from which to find the remainder after dividing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341				0	cy	\<emph\>Divisor\</emph\> is the number by which to divide the specified value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374				0	cy	The value 17 in the Dividend field is to be divided by the divisor -1.4. -1.2 will be returned as the remainder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
