helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3158414				0	cy	Grade				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152820				0	cy	Age				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154866				0	cy	Distance to School				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150471				0	cy	Weight				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153920				0	cy	14				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148429				0	cy	>600				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152588				0	cy	15				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3083286				0	cy	16				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163823				0	cy	DCOUNT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145083				0	cy	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149282				0	cy	The formula in cell B16 is =DCOUNT(A1:E10;0;A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150962				0	cy	Database Function Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155837				0	cy	The following are the parameter definitions for all database functions:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149453				0	cy	\<emph\>Database\</emph\> is the cell range defining the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272	86			0	cy	\<emph\>Database field\</emph\> specifies the column where the function operates on after the search criteria of the first parameter is applied and the data rows are selected. It is not related to the search criteria itself. Use the number 0 to specify the whole data range. \<variable id=\"quotes\"\>To reference a column by means of the column header name, place quotation marks around the header name. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147083				0	cy	\<emph\>Search criteria\</emph\> is the cell range containing search criteria. If you write several criteria in one row they are connected by AND. If you write the criteria in different rows they are connected by OR. Empty cells in the search criteria range will be ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150882				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DCOUNT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150882				0	cy	DCOUNT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBANZAHL\"\>DCOUNT counts the number of rows (records) in a database that match the specified search criteria and contain numerical values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156099				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153218				0	cy	DCOUNT(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153273	187			0	cy	For the Database Field parameter you can enter a cell to specify the column, or enter the number 0 for the entire database. The parameter cannot be empty. \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/01/04060101.xhp#quotes\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154743				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153623				0	cy	In the example above (scroll up, please), we want to know how many children have to travel more than 600 meters to school. The result is to be stored in cell B16. Set the cursor in cell B16. Enter the formula =DCOUNT(A1:E10;0;A13:E14) in B16. The \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> helps you to input ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149142				0	cy	\<emph\>Database\</emph\> is the range of data to be evaluated, including its headers: in this case A1:E10. \<emph\>Database field\</emph\> specifies the column for the search criteria: in this case, the whole database. \<emph\>Search criteria\</emph\> is the range where you can enter the search parameters: in this case, A13:E14.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652				0	cy	To learn how many children in second grade are over 7 years of age, delete the entry >600 in cell D14 and enter "2" in cell B14 under Grade, and enter >7 in cell C14 to the right. The result is 2. Two children are in second grade and over 7 years of age. As both criteria are in the same row, they are connected by AND.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156123				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DCOUNTA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156123				0	cy	DCOUNTA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBANZAHL2\"\>DCOUNTA counts the number of rows (records) in a database that match the specified search conditions, and contain numeric or alphanumeric values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146893				0	cy	DCOUNTA(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153982				0	cy	In the example above (scroll up, please), you can search for the number of children whose name starts with an E or a subsequent letter. Edit the formula in B16 to read =DCOUNTA(A1:E10;0;A13:E14). Delete the old search criteria and enter >=E under \<emph\>Name\</emph\> in field A14. The result is 5. If you now delete all number values for Greta in row 8, the result changes to 4. Row 8 is no longer included in the count because it does not contain any values. The name Greta is text, not a value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147256				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DGET function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147256				0	cy	DGET				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBAUSZUG\"\>DGET returns the contents of the referenced cell in a database which matches the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> In case of an error, the function returns either #VALUE! for no row found, or Err502 for more than one cell found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159344				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154696				0	cy	DGET(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153909				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	cy	In the above example (scroll up, please), we want to determine what grade a child is in, whose name was entered in cell A14. The formula is entered in cell B16 and differs slightly from the earlier examples because only one column (one database field) can be entered for \<emph\>Database field\</emph\>. Enter the following formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096				0	cy	=DGET(A1:E10;"Grade";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	cy	Enter the name Frank in A14, and you see the result 2. Frank is in second grade. Enter "Age" instead of "Grade" and you will get Frank's age.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	cy	Or enter the value 11 in cell C14 only, and delete the other entries in this row. Edit the formula in B16 as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149912				0	cy	=DGET(A1:E10;"Name";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	cy	Instead of the grade, the name is queried. The answer appears at once: Daniel is the only child aged 11.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149766				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DMAX function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	cy	DMAX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154903				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMAX\"\>DMAX returns the maximum content of a cell (field) in a database (all records) that matches the specified search conditions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	cy	DMAX(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145420				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148442				0	cy	To find out how much the heaviest child in each grade weighed in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148804				0	cy	=DMAX(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	cy	Under 'Grade', enter 1, 2, 3, and so on, one after the other. After entering a grade number, the weight of the heaviest child in that grade appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159141				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DMIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159141				0	cy	DMIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154261				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMIN\"\>DMIN returns the minimum content of a cell (field) in a database that matches the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147238				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148479				0	cy	DMIN(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151050				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	cy	To find the shortest distance to school for the children in each grade in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149161				0	cy	=DMIN(A1:E10;"Distance to School";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	cy	In row 14, under Grade, enter 1, 2, 3, and so on, one after the other. The shortest distance to school for each grade appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154274				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DAVERAGE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154274				0	cy	DAVERAGE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166453				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMITTELWERT\"\>DAVERAGE returns the average of the values of all cells (fields) in all rows (database records) that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146955				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150710				0	cy	DAVERAGE(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152943				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149104				0	cy	To find the average weight of all children of the same age in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153688				0	cy	=DAVERAGE(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155587				0	cy	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. The average weight of all children of the same age appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159269				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DPRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159269				0	cy	DPRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152879				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBPRODUKT\"\>DPRODUCT multiplies all cells of a data range where the cell contents match the search criteria.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149966				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154854				0	cy	DPRODUCT(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149802				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148986				0	cy	With the birthday party example above (scroll up, please), there is no meaningful application of this function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148462				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEV function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148462				0	cy	DSTDEV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABW\"\>DSTDEV calculates the standard deviation of a population based on a sample, using the numbers in a database column that match the given conditions.\</ahelp\> The records are treated as a sample of data. That means that the children in the example represent a cross section of all children. Note that a representative result can not be obtained from a sample of less than one thousand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149427				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148661				0	cy	DSTDEV(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153945				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149934				0	cy	To find the standard deviation of the weight for all children of the same age in the example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630				0	cy	=DSTDEV(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	cy	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. The result shown is the standard deviation of the weight of all children of this age.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150429				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEVP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150429				0	cy	DSTDEVP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145598				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABWN\"\>DSTDEVP calculates the standard deviation of a population based on all cells of a data range which match the search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as the whole population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145307				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	cy	DSTDEVP(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153322				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	cy	To find the standard deviation of the weight for all children of the same age at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148411				0	cy	=DSTDEVP(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	cy	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. The result is the standard deviation of the weight for all same-aged children whose weight was checked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154794				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154794				0	cy	DSUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149591				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSUMME\"\>DSUM returns the total of all cells in a database field in all rows (records) that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146128				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150989				0	cy	DSUM(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159079				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152766				0	cy	To find the length of the combined distance to school of all children at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please) who are in second grade, enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151312				0	cy	=DSUM(A1:E10;"Distance to School";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596				0	cy	Enter "2" in row 14 under "Grade". The sum (1950) of the distances to school of all the children who are in second grade is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155614				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DVAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155614				0	cy	DVAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154418				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZ\"\>DVAR returns the variance of all cells of a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as a sample of data. A representative result cannot be obtained from a sample population of less than one thousand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154825				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	cy	DVAR(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153701				0	cy	To find the variance of the weight of all children of the same age of the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153676				0	cy	=DVAR(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153798				0	cy	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. You will see as a result the variance of the weight values for all children of this age.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153880				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DVARP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	cy	DVARP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155119				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZEN\"\>DVARP calculates the variance of all cell values in a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records are from the example are treated as an entire population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145774				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153776				0	cy	DVARP(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147099				0	cy	To find the variance of the weight for all children of the same age at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	cy	=DVARP(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146902				0	cy	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. The variance of the weight values for all children of this age attending Joe's birthday party appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\01120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Page Preview				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\01120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155829				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0210.xhp\" name=\"Page View Object Bar\"\>Page View Object Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	WEEKNUM_ADD 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166443				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKNUM_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166443				0	cy	\<variable id=\"weeknumadd\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknumadd.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM_ADD\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WEEKNUM\"\>The result indicates the number of the calendar week for a \<emph\>Date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DD				0	cy	The WEEKNUM_ADD function is designed to calculate week numbers exactly as Microsoft Excel does. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknum.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM\</link\> function, or format your date cells using the WW formatting code, when you need ISO 8601 week numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153745				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3153685				0	cy	WEEKNUM_ADD(Date;Return type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3159277				0	cy	\<emph\>Date\</emph\>: the date within the calendar week.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	cy	\<emph\>Return type\</emph\>: 1 for week beginning on a Sunday, 2 for week beginning on a Monday.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152886				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3149973				0	cy	In which week number does 12.24.2001 fall?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3149914				0	cy	=WEEKNUM_ADD("24.12.2001";1) returns 52.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Text Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145389				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard;text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145389				0	cy	Text Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3152986				0	cy	\<variable id=\"texttext\"\>This section contains descriptions of the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> functions. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149384				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>ARABIC function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149384				0	cy	ARABIC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153558				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARABISCH\"\>Calculates the value of a Roman number. The value range must be between 0 and 3999.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153011				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155523				0	cy	ARABIC (Text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193	243			0	cy	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the text that represents a Roman number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155758				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154621	245			0	cy	Arabic("MXIV") returns 1014				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147553	246			0	cy	Arabic("MMII") returns 2002				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id9942014				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id9694814				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153072				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>BASE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153072				0	cy	BASE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153289				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BASIS\"\>Converts a positive integer to a specified base into a text from the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#zahlensystem\" name=\"numbering system\"\>numbering system\</link\>.\</ahelp\> The digits 0-9 and the letters A-Z are used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146097				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155743				0	cy	BASE(Number; Radix; [Minimum length])				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151339	217			0	cy	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the positive integer to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262	218			0	cy	\<emph\>radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148746	219			0	cy	\<emph\>Minimum length\</emph\> (optional) determines the minimum length of the character sequence that has been created. If the text is shorter than the indicated minimum length, zeros are added to the left of the string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146323				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156399				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>decimal system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399	221			0	cy	BASE(17;10;4) returns 0017 in the decimal system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157871				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>binary system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	222			0	cy	BASE(17;2) returns 10001 in the binary system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145226				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>hexadecimal system; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145226	223			0	cy	BASE(255;16;4) returns 00FF in the hexadecimal system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149321				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>CHAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149321				0	cy	CHAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEICHEN\"\>Converts a number into a character according to the current code table.\</ahelp\> The number can be a two-digit or three-digit integer number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149945				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145634				0	cy	CHAR(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906	205			0	cy	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is a number between 1 and 255 representing the code value for the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152982				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149890	208			0	cy	CHAR(100) returns the character "d".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149009				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>CLEAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149009				0	cy	CLEAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150482				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SAEUBERN\"\>All non-printing characters are removed from the string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147472				0	cy	CLEAN(text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150695	136			0	cy	\<emph\>text\</emph\> refers to the text from which to remove all non-printable characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155498				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>CODE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155498				0	cy	CODE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CODE\"\>Returns a numeric code for the first character in a text string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155830				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149188				0	cy	CODE(Text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383	7			0	cy	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the text for which the code of the first character is to be found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154394				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159209	9			0	cy	CODE("Hieronymus") returns 72, CODE("hieroglyphic") returns 104.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150280				0	cy	The code used here does not refer to ASCII, but to the code table currently loaded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>CONCATENATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	cy	CONCATENATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154524				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERKETTEN\"\>Combines several text strings into one string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149542				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155954				0	cy	CONCATENATE(Text 1;...;Text 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146847	171			0	cy	\<emph\>Text 1; text 2; ...\</emph\> represent up to 30 text passages which are to be combined into one string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153110				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150008	173			0	cy	CONCATENATE("Good ";"Morning ";"Mrs. ";"Doe") returns \<emph\>Good Morning Mrs. Doe\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145166				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DECIMAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145166				0	cy	DECIMAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156361				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DEZIMAL\"\>Converts text with characters from a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#zahlensystem\" name=\"number system\"\>number system\</link\> to a positive integer in the base radix given.\</ahelp\> The radix must be in the range 2 to 36. Spaces and tabs are ignored. The\<emph\> text\</emph\> field is not case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157994				0	cy	If the radix is 16, a leading x or X or 0x or 0X, and an appended h or H, is disregarded. If the radix is 2, an appended b or B is disregarded. Other characters that do not belong to the number system generate an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150014				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154328				0	cy	DECIMAL(Text; Radix)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150128	230			0	cy	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text to be converted. To differentiate between a hexadecimal number, such as A1 and the reference to cell A1, you must place the number in quotation marks, for example, "A1" or "FACE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	231			0	cy	\<emph\>radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156062				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145355	233			0	cy	DECIMAL("17";10) returns 17.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622	234			0	cy	DECIMAL("FACE";16) returns 64206.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151015	235			0	cy	DECIMAL("0101";2) returns 5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148402				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>DOLLAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148402				0	cy	DOLLAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049	12			0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DM\"\>Converts a number to an amount in the currency format, rounded to a specified decimal place.\</ahelp\> In the \<emph\>value\</emph\> field enter the number to be converted to currency. Optionally, you may enter the number of decimal places in the \<emph\>decimals\</emph\> field. If no value is specified, all numbers in currency format will be displayed with two decimal places. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	cy	You set the currency format in your system settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150569				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	cy	DOLLAR(value; decimals)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299	15			0	cy	\<emph\>value\</emph\> is a number, a reference to a cell containing a number, or a formula which returns a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	16			0	cy	\<emph\>decimals\</emph\> is the optional number of decimal places.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149030				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546	18			0	cy	DOLLAR(255) returns $255.00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635	19			0	cy	DOLLAR(367.456;2) returns $367.46. Use the decimal separator that corresponds to the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"current locale setting\"\>current locale setting\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150685				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>EXACT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	cy	EXACT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_IDENTISCH\"\>Compares two text strings and returns TRUE if they are identical.\</ahelp\> This function is case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152817				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594				0	cy	EXACT(text_1;text_2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153224	82			0	cy	\<emph\>text_1\</emph\> refers to the first text to compare.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148637	83			0	cy	\<emph\>text_2\</emph\> is the second text to compare.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149777				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
