helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154359				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_T\"\>This function converts a number to a blank text string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155858				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	cy	T(value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154726				0	cy	\<emph\>value\</emph\> is the value to be converted. Also, a reference can be used as a parameter. If the referenced cell includes a number or a formula containing a numerical result, the result will be an empty string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155544				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151062	146			0	cy	T(12345) becomes an empty string "", if 12345 is formatted as a number. T("12345") returns 12345.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147132				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>TEXT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
