helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	cy	Right-To-Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065A				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SheetRightToLeft\"\>Changes the orientation of the current sheet to Right-To-Left if \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\"\>CTL\</link\> support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	WORKDAY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	cy	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>Workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>Start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	cy	WORKDAY (Start date;Days;Holidays)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	cy	\<emph\>Start date\</emph\>: the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	cy	\<emph\>Days\</emph\>: the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	cy	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\>: list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	cy	What date comes 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "12/1/2001" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "12/24/2001", "12/25/2001", "12/26/2001", "12/31/2001", "1/1/2002".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	cy	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 12/28/2001. Format the serial date number as a date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	YEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
