helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	cy	GAUSS(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153228	80			0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value for which the integral value of the normalized standard distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150691				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867	82			0	cy	GAUSS(0.19) = 0.08				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594	83			0	cy	GAUSS(0.0375) = 0.01				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148425				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>GEOMEAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148425				0	cy	GEOMEAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GEOMITTEL\"\>Returns the geometric mean of a sample.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147167				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153720				0	cy	GEOMEAN(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585	89			0	cy	\<emph\>Number 1, Number 2,...Number 30\</emph\> are numeric arguments or ranges that represent a random sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	92			0	cy	GEOMEAN(23; 46; 69) = 41.79. The geometric mean value of this random sample is therefore 41.79.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152966				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>TRIMMEAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152966				0	cy	TRIMMEAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GESTUTZTMITTEL\"\>Returns the mean of a data set without the Alpha percent of data at the margins.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149281				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154821				0	cy	TRIMMEAN(Data; Alpha)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155834	98			0	cy	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156304	99			0	cy	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is the percentage of the marginal data that will not be taken into consideration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151180				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	101			0	cy	=TRIMMEAN(A1:A50; 0.1) calculates the mean value of numbers in A1:A50, without taking into consideration the 5 percent of the values representing the highest values and the 5 percent of the values representing the lowest ones. The percentage numbers refer to the amount of the untrimmed mean value, not to the number of summands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153216				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>ZTEST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153216				0	cy	ZTEST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3150758				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GTEST\"\>Returns the two-tailed P value of a z test with standard distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150872				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153274				0	cy	ZTEST(Data; Number; Sigma)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156109	107			0	cy	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array of the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977	108			0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154740	109			0	cy	\<emph\>Sigma\</emph\> (optional) is the standard deviation of the total population. If this argument is missing, the standard deviation of the sample in question will be processed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153623				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>HARMEAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153623				0	cy	HARMEAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155102				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HARMITTEL\"\>Returns the harmonic mean of a data set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146900				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	cy	HARMEAN(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154303	117			0	cy	\<emph\>Number 1,Number 2,...Number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 values or ranges, that can be used to calculate the harmonic mean.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159179				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093	120			0	cy	HARMEAN(23;46;69) = 37.64. The harmonic mean of this random sample is thus 37.64				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>HYPGEOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	cy	HYPGEOMDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3159341				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HYPGEOMVERT\"\>Returns the hypergeometric distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154697				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	cy	HYPGEOMDIST(X; N_sample; Successes; N_population)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154933	126			0	cy	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of results achieved in the random sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153106	127			0	cy	\<emph\>N_sample\</emph\> is the size of the random sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146992	128			0	cy	\<emph\>Successes\</emph\> is the number of possible results in the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	129			0	cy	\<emph\>N_population \</emph\>is the size of the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150529				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154904	131			0	cy	=HYPGEOMDIST(2; 2; 90; 100) yields 0.81. If 90 out of 100 pieces of buttered toast fall from the table and hit the floor with the buttered side first, then if 2 pieces of buttered toast are dropped from the table, the probability is 81%, that both will strike buttered side first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Freeze				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150517				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Freeze\"\>Freeze\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FreezePanes\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Divides the sheet at the top left corner of the active cell and the area to the top left is no longer scrollable.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
