helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153250				0	cy	RANK(Value; Data; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154543	6			0	cy	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value, whose rank is to be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149130	7			0	cy	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215	8			0	cy	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the sequence order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id9305398				0	cy	Type = 0 means descending from the last item of the array to the first (this is the default), 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id9996948				0	cy	Type = 1 means ascending from the first item of the range to the last.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143223				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919	10			0	cy	=RANK(A10; A1:A50) returns the ranking of the value in A10 in value range A1:A50. If \<emph\>Value\</emph\> does not exist within the range an error message is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
