helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	cy	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	cy	PERMUTATIONA(11;2) returns 121.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	cy	PERMUTATIONA(6; 3) returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152952				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>PROB function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	cy	PROB				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154110				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHRSCHBEREICH\"\>Returns the probability that values in a range are between two limits.\</ahelp\> If there is no \<emph\>End\</emph\> value, this function calculates the probability based on the principle that the Data values are equal to the value of \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146810				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330				0	cy	PROB(Data; Probability; Start; End)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	cy	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	cy	\<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	cy	\<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	cy	\<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	cy	=PROB(A1:A50; B1:B50; 50; 60) returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941				0	cy	WEIBULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	cy	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	cy	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	cy	\<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the Alpha parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	cy	\<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the Beta parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	cy	\<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function. If C equals 0 the form of the function is calculated, if C equals 1 the distribution is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	cy	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	cy	=WEIBULL(2; 1; 1; 1) returns 0.86.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Trace Error				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153561				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tracing errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error tracing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030600.xhp\" name=\"Trace Error\"\>Trace Error\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	cy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowErrors\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Draws tracer arrows to all precedent cells which cause an error value in a selected cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
