helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Consolidating Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>values; consolidating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; merging ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	cy	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	cy	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	cy	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	cy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	cy	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	cy	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	cy	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	cy	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	cy	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	cy	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	cy	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	cy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	cy	Additional Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	cy	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	cy	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	cy	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	cy	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	cy	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	cy	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	cy	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
