helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	cy	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	cy	Mark a single cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	cy	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	cy	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	cy	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	cy	Select various dispersed cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	cy	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	cy	Switch marking mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	cy	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
