helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	cy	If you want to insert a formula into a text document, and you already know the correct writing, you can proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	cy	Write the formula into your text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	cy	Select the formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	cy	Choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154767				0	cy	Inserting a Formula using a Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	cy	If you want to use the $[officename] Math interface to edit a formula, choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\> without any text selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	cy	The cursor waits in the Commands window and you can type the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
