helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Libraries, Modules and Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147317				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01020500.xhp\" name=\"Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\"\>Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	cy	The following describes the basic use of libraries, modules and dialogs in $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	cy	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	cy	Libraries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	cy	Libraries serve as a tool for organizing modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	cy	A library can contain up to 16,000 modules.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	cy	Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	cy	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	cy	Dialog Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	cy	Dialog modules contain dialog definitions, including the dialog box properties, the properties of each dialog element and the events assigned. Since a dialog module can only contain a single dialog, they are often referred to as "dialogs".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Time Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
