helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>If statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090101.xhp\" name=\"If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\"\>If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	cy	Defines one or more statement blocks that you only want to execute if a given condition is True.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	cy	If condition=true Then Statement block [ElseIf condition=true Then] Statement block [Else] Statement block End If				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	cy	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	cy	The \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement executes program blocks depending on given conditions. When $[officename] Basic encounters an \<emph\>If\</emph\> statement, the condition is tested. If the condition is True, all subsequent statements up to the next \<emph\>Else\</emph\> or \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement are executed. If the condition is False, and an \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement follows, $[officename] Basic tests the next condition and executes the following statements if the condition is True. If False, the program continues either with the next \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> or \<emph\>Else\</emph\> statement. Statements following \<emph\>Else\</emph\> are executed only if none of the previously tested conditions were True. After all conditions are evaluated, and the corresponding statements executed, the program continues with the statement following \<emph\>EndIf\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	cy	You can nest multiple \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	cy	\<emph\>Else\</emph\> and \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statements are optional.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152939				0	cy	You can use \<emph\>GoTo\</emph\> and \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> to jump out of an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> block, but not to jump into an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	cy	The following example enables you to enter the expiration date of a product, and determines if the expiration date has passed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152576				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	cy	Sub ExampleIfThenDate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	cy	Dim sDate as String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	cy	Dim sToday as String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	cy	sDate = InputBox("Enter the expiration date (MM.DD.YYYY)")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	cy	sDate = Right$(sDate, 4) + Mid$(sDate, 4, 2) + Left$(sDate, 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	cy	sToday = Date$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	cy	sToday = Right$(sToday, 4)+ Mid$(sToday, 4, 2) + Left$(sToday, 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	cy	If sDate < sToday Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601				0	cy	MsgBox "The expiration date has passed"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	cy	ElseIf sDate > sToday Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146912				0	cy	MsgBox "The expiration date has not yet passed"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	cy	Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	cy	MsgBox "The expiration date is today"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	cy	End If				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	cy	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
