helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366	10			0	cy	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>Position for the next writing or reading. Position can be a number between 1 and 2,147,483,647. According to the file type, the position indicates the number of the record (files in the Random mode) or the byte position (files in the Binary, Output, Append or Input mode). The first byte in a file is position 1, the second byte is position 2, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
