helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Print Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147230				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>Print statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010103.xhp\" name=\"Print Statement [Runtime]\"\>Print Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	cy	Prints the specified strings or numeric expressions in a dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	4			0	cy	Print Expression1[{;|,} [Spc(Number As Integer);] [Tab(pos As Integer);] [Expression2[...]] 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	cy	Parameter:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	cy	\<emph\>Expression\</emph\>: Any numeric or string expression to be printed. Multiple expressions can be separated by a semicolon. If separated by a comma, the expressions are indented to the next tab stop. The tab stops cannot be adjusted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	cy	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>: Number of spaces to be inserted by the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	cy	\<emph\>Pos\</emph\>: Spaces are inserted until the specified position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	cy	If a semicolon or comma appears after the last expression to be printed, $[officename] Basic stores the text in an internal buffer and continues program execution without printing. When another Print statement without a semicolon or comma at the end is encountered, all text to be printed is printed at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	cy	Positive numeric expressions are printed with a leading space. Negative expressions are printed with a leading minus sign. If a certain range is exceeded for floating-point values, the respective numeric expression is printed in exponential notation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	cy	If the expression to be printed exceeds a certain length, the display will automatically wrap to the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	cy	You can insert the Tab function, enclosed by semicolons, between arguments to indent the output to a specific position, or you can use the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function to insert a specified number of spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146912				0	cy	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	cy	Sub ExamplePrint				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764				0	cy	Print "ABC"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	cy	Print "ABC","123"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	cy	end Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	$[officename] Basic Glossary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Basic Glossary\"\>$[officename] Basic Glossary\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	cy	This glossary explains some technical terms that you may come across when working with $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155133				0	cy	Decimal Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156443				0	cy	When converting numbers, $[officename] Basic uses the locale settings of the system for determining the type of decimal and thousand separator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	cy	The behavior has an effect on both the implicit conversion ( 1 + "2.3" = 3.3 ) as well as the runtime function \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03102700.xhp\" name=\"IsNumeric\"\>IsNumeric\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155854				0	cy	Colors				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	cy	In $[officename] Basic, colors are treated as long integer value. The return value of color queries is also always a long integer value. When defining properties, colors can be specified using their RGB code that is converted to a long integer value using the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010305.xhp\" name=\"RGB function\"\>RGB function\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	cy	Measurement Units				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145801				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>twips; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	cy	Twips				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	cy	A twip is a screen-independent unit which is used to define the uniform position and size of screen elements on all display systems. A twip is 1/1440th of an inch or 1/20 of a printer's point. There are 1440 twips to an inch or about 567 twips to a centimeter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153159				0	cy	URL Notation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	cy	URLs (\<emph\>Uniform Resource Locators\</emph\>) are used to determine the location of a resource like a file in a file system, typically inside a network environment. A URL consists of a protocol specifier, a host specifier and a file and path specifier:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	cy	\<emph\>protocol\</emph\>://\<emph\>host.name\</emph\>/\<emph\>path/to/the/file.html\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3168612				0	cy	The most common usage of URLs is on the internet when specifying web pages. Example for protocols are \<emph\>http\</emph\>, \<emph\>ftp\</emph\>, or \<emph\>file\</emph\>. The \<emph\>file\</emph\> protocol specifier is used when referring to a file on the local file system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150324	110			0	cy	URL notation does not allow certain special characters to be used. These are either replaced by other characters or encoded. A slash (\<emph\>/\</emph\>) is used as a path separator. For example, a file referred to as \<emph\>C:\\My File.sxw\</emph\> on the local host in "Windows notation" becomes \<emph\>file:///C|/My%20File.sxw\</emph\> in URL notation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020415.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	FileExists Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020415.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148946				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>FileExists function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020415.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020415.xhp\" name=\"FileExists Function [Runtime]\"\>FileExists Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020415.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	cy	Determines if a file or a directory is available on the data medium.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020415.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150447				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
