helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	cy	Cos Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154923				0	cy	\<bookmark_value\>Cos function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154923				0	cy	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080102.xhp\" name=\"Cos Function [Runtime]\"\>Cos Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	cy	Calculates the cosine of an angle. The angle is specified in radians. The result lies between -1 and 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	cy	Using the angle Alpha, the Cos-Function calculates the ratio of the length of the side that is adjacent to the angle, divided by the length of the hypotenuse in a right-angled triangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154141				0	cy	Cos(Alpha) = Adjacent/Hypotenuse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	cy	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	cy	Cos (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156214				0	cy	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	cy	Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	cy	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	cy	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that specifies an angle in radians that you want to calculate the cosine for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	cy	To convert degrees to radians, multiply degrees by pi/180. To convert radians to degrees, multiply radians by 180/pi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	cy	degree=(radian*180)/pi				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	cy	radian=(degree*pi)/180				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	cy	Pi is here the fixed circle constant with the rounded value 3.14159...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
